MAN: Yeah.

4
00:02:28.482 --> 00:02:30.450
(MAN SPEAKING SPANISH)

5
00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.201
(IN ENGLISH)
This is the Cuban spirit.

6
00:02:32.944 --> 00:02:34.321
(DOM SPEAKS SPANISH)

7
00:02:35.572 --> 00:02:37.791
Dom. Dom.
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

8
00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:44.465
(ENGINE REVVING)
(ALL CHEERING)

9
00:02:50.128 --> 00:02:53.177
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

10
00:02:53.256 --> 00:02:54.929
(IN ENGLISH) You know
I can't make a living without my car.

11
00:02:55.008 --> 00:02:56.555
Not my problem. bro.

12
00:02:57.552 --> 00:03:01.227
Dominic Toretto. I heard about you.
Welcome to my island.

13
00:03:01.473 --> 00:03:02.850
Why you hookin' up my cousin's car?

14
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.352
He needed money. I gave it to him.

15
00:03:05.435 --> 00:03:07.608
He can't pay. I take the car.

16
00:03:07.688 --> 00:03:08.780
I just need a few more days.

17
00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:10.323
"Few more days" wasn't part of the deal.

18
00:03:11.108 --> 00:03:14.362
Come on. You make a deal.
you gotta live up to it.

19
00:03:14.444 --> 00:03:16.993
You make a deal. you gonna live up to it.

20
00:03:17.906 --> 00:03:19.328
"Gonna" live up to it?

21
00:03:21.535 --> 00:03:23.128
Oh. so you're one of those types.

22
00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:26.756
You take everyone's ride.
and then ship it back to the States?

23
00:03:26.832 --> 00:03:28.926
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

24
00:03:29.418 --> 00:03:30.385
(IN ENGLISH)
You watch your mouth.

25
00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.677
(CHUCKLES)

26
00:03:32.796 --> 00:03:34.093
Now you got a problem.

27
00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:39.060
I'm gonna keep it about the cars.

28
00:03:39.302 --> 00:03:42.146
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

29
00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:43.565
(IN ENGLISH) You want a car.
get it the right way.

30
00:03:44.141 --> 00:03:45.142
How?

31
00:03:45.684 --> 00:03:46.901
Race for it.

32
00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.070
I already own it. bro.

33
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:51.448
Not that car.

34
00:03:52.983 --> 00:03:54.985
Mine.
(CROWD EXCLAIMING)

35
00:03:55.444 --> 00:03:58.197
Dom. his car is the fastest
car on the island.

36
00:03:58.488 --> 00:03:59.990
Do you know what he has under that hood?

37
00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.459
He knows it doesn't matter
what's under a hood.

38
00:04:03.326 --> 00:04:06.296
The only thing that matters is
who's behind the wheel.

39
00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:07.463
You think so?

40
00:04:07.748 --> 00:04:08.965
I know so.

41
00:04:09.332 --> 00:04:11.005
Then race his car.

42
00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.509
And we ain't racing
no quarter-mile. here.

43
00:04:16.006 --> 00:04:17.474
We race the Cuban mile.

44
00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:20.139
Done.

45
00:04:20.218 --> 00:04:22.266
(CROWD CHEERING)

46
00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:25.686
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

47
00:04:35.066 --> 00:04:37.034
I appreciate what you're trying to do.

48
00:04:37.527 --> 00:04:39.529
but my car is the slowest
car on the island.

49
00:04:42.616 --> 00:04:43.833
Was.

50
00:04:44.701 --> 00:04:46.703
Pull the seats. the doors. the battery...

51
00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:49.377
If it ain't the motor. take it off.

52
00:04:50.248 --> 00:04:51.374
Laughing gas?

53
00:04:51.708 --> 00:04:53.710
Nah. Fed.
This is Cuban NOS.

54
00:04:54.377 --> 00:04:55.629
You guys are crazy.

55
00:04:57.631 --> 00:04:58.803
What are you doing?

56
00:04:58.882 --> 00:05:02.512
DOM: Poor man's turbo.
Pull the vacuum line and hold on.

57
00:05:03.053 --> 00:05:05.852
Old trick that Buster used to play.
in case of emergencies.

58
00:05:06.473 --> 00:05:08.851
You know that's way
too much boost for that engine.

59
00:05:09.142 --> 00:05:10.189
DOM: It's gonna be fast.

60
00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:11.607
It's gonna be a bomb.

61
00:05:12.896 --> 00:05:14.523
Only needs to go a mile.

62
00:05:19.694 --> 00:05:21.571
(CROWD CHEERING)

63
00:05:24.407 --> 00:05:26.159
(ENGINES REVVING)

64
00:05:41.299 --> 00:05:43.347
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

65
00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:57.778
<i>Vámonos!</i>

66
00:06:25.886 --> 00:06:26.887
(TIRES SQUEALING)

67
00:06:30.557 --> 00:06:31.558
(LAUGHING)

68
00:06:35.604 --> 00:06:37.948
(IN ENGLISH) That car belongs
in the trash. bro!

69
00:06:53.204 --> 00:06:55.423
(TIRES SQUEALING)
(HORN BLARING)

70
00:07:10.138 --> 00:07:11.185
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

71
00:07:12.849 --> 00:07:14.601
(CHILDREN CHEERING)

72
00:07:27.656 --> 00:07:28.623
FERNANDO:
Where are they going?

73
00:07:28.698 --> 00:07:29.870
LETTY: I don't know.
Let's go!

74
00:07:43.964 --> 00:07:44.965
(CELL PHONE BEEPS)

75
00:07:45.048 --> 00:07:46.049
Ghost him.

76
00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:48.393
MAN: <i>Sí.</i>
(PEOPLE YELLING)

77
00:08:05.902 --> 00:08:07.700
<i>Adiós.</i> Toretto!

78
00:08:11.658 --> 00:08:13.035
Okay. Buster.

79
00:08:13.702 --> 00:08:15.170
Let's see if this works.

80
00:08:16.913 --> 00:08:18.631
(TIRES SQUEALING)
(ENGINE REVVING)

81
00:08:23.086 --> 00:08:24.303
That's impossible.

82
00:08:56.411 --> 00:08:58.334
(ALL CHEERING)

83
00:09:03.043 --> 00:09:04.044
(GLASS SHATTERING)

84
00:09:06.337 --> 00:09:07.884
(TIRES SQUEAL)

85
00:09:24.814 --> 00:09:26.316
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

86
00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:36.997
(EXCLAIMS)

87
00:09:39.996 --> 00:09:41.339
(CHEERING)

88
00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.547
(IN ENGLISH) Look out!

89
00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.852
(ALL CONTINUE CHEERING)

90
00:10:39.722 --> 00:10:40.769
A deal's a deal.

91
00:10:42.433 --> 00:10:43.605
You won my car.

92
00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.397
And you earned my respect.

93
00:11:02.245 --> 00:11:03.588
Keep your car.

94
00:11:04.706 --> 00:11:06.424
Your respect is good enough for me.

95
00:11:11.921 --> 00:11:13.138
DOM: Yo. cousin...

96
00:11:14.465 --> 00:11:15.842
Sorry about your car.

97
00:11:20.930 --> 00:11:23.433
Yours was too slow for a Toretto. anyway.

98
00:11:23.516 --> 00:11:26.190
Your Impala?
Are you serious?

99
00:11:27.437 --> 00:11:29.360
(ALL CHEERING)

100
00:12:13.274 --> 00:12:14.821
Look at that smile.

101
00:12:15.318 --> 00:12:16.945
I love it when you smile.

102
00:12:17.028 --> 00:12:18.325
You make me happy.

103
00:12:19.155 --> 00:12:21.658
Mmm. I think this place makes you happy.

104
00:12:24.077 --> 00:12:25.499
It's like it speaks to you.

105
00:12:29.082 --> 00:12:32.382
You remember that guy.
the racer and his dad?

106
00:12:33.461 --> 00:12:34.713
The one with the boat engine under the hood?

107
00:12:34.796 --> 00:12:35.797
Yeah!

108
00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.553
- Yes.
- Of course.

109
00:12:37.632 --> 00:12:40.556
I was looking at them. and I...

110
00:12:41.135 --> 00:12:42.603
And I couldn't help but to imagine

111
00:12:42.679 --> 00:12:45.307
what you'd be like if you were a dad.

112
00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:49.944
No. no. no!
I'm not pregnant.

113
00:12:54.065 --> 00:12:55.191
Is that what you want?

114
00:12:56.234 --> 00:12:58.657
It's not about what I want or
what you want.

115
00:12:59.404 --> 00:13:02.032
It's about why we haven't
asked the question.

116
00:13:19.757 --> 00:13:21.384
(ENGINE CRANKS SLOWLY)

117
00:13:25.805 --> 00:13:27.227
(SPEAKING SPANISH)

118
00:13:28.975 --> 00:13:30.727
- (IN ENGLISH)What?
- You need a hand?

119
00:13:31.978 --> 00:13:33.230
Yeah. I think I do.

120
00:13:34.063 --> 00:13:36.316
- Sounds like you're not getting any fuel.
- Yeah?

121
00:13:36.399 --> 00:13:38.322
Probably the shut-off solenoid.

122
00:13:38.735 --> 00:13:40.237
Let's see if we can get some power to it.

123
00:13:42.864 --> 00:13:44.366
What brings you to Cuba?

124
00:13:46.117 --> 00:13:48.211
The same thing that brings
everyone else to Cuba.

125
00:13:49.245 --> 00:13:51.668
Culture. people. the beauty.

126
00:13:52.415 --> 00:13:53.758
What brings you to Cuba?

127
00:13:54.292 --> 00:13:56.636
- Work.
- Must be casual Friday.

128
00:13:58.463 --> 00:13:59.931
How's that honeymoon going. Dom?

129
00:14:05.762 --> 00:14:07.685
Your fuel relay is missing.

130
00:14:09.807 --> 00:14:11.104
I know.

131
00:14:14.687 --> 00:14:16.360
I love to play games.

132
00:14:16.439 --> 00:14:17.986
I've beaten the best of 'em.

133
00:14:19.067 --> 00:14:21.411
But I'm kind of in a rush.
so if you've got something to say to me...

134
00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:23.864
Oh. this is a very different game.
that I can assure you.

135
00:14:24.947 --> 00:14:29.202
This... There's something
much greater at work here.

136
00:14:29.994 --> 00:14:30.995
This is fate.

137
00:14:31.746 --> 00:14:33.339
I choose to make my own fate.

138
00:14:33.581 --> 00:14:34.958
Not today.

139
00:14:35.625 --> 00:14:38.629
Is this the road you take to
your apartment every morning?

140
00:14:38.795 --> 00:14:41.799
What else is different. Dom?
Was Santiago's closed?

141
00:14:41.964 --> 00:14:44.058
Did you have to cross two blocks to
go get your Cuban coffees?

142
00:14:44.133 --> 00:14:46.431
What is it. black. no sugar?

143
00:14:47.845 --> 00:14:48.937
Yeah.

144
00:14:49.097 --> 00:14:51.395
I put a lot of work into
getting you here today.

145
00:14:52.308 --> 00:14:53.901
Well. now that I'm here. what do you want?

146
00:14:54.352 --> 00:14:55.649
I want you to work for me.

147
00:14:57.313 --> 00:14:58.314
Work for you?

148
00:14:58.815 --> 00:15:00.988
Oh. I could've saved you
a lot of time. then.

149
00:15:01.442 --> 00:15:02.819
See. I don't work for anyone.

150
00:15:03.444 --> 00:15:05.367
You can't walk away from this. Dom.

151
00:15:05.446 --> 00:15:07.949
We're gonna have this conversation.
one way or the other.

152
00:15:09.325 --> 00:15:11.168
You see. that's the funny thing about fate.

153
00:15:12.036 --> 00:15:13.208
It's cunning.

154
00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.173
It can bring you beautiful things.

155
00:15:15.248 --> 00:15:17.421
and it can also bring
you moments like this.

156
00:15:31.347 --> 00:15:33.725
Oh. you're gonna want to work for me.

157
00:15:34.350 --> 00:15:35.852
You're gonna betray your brothers.

158
00:15:35.935 --> 00:15:38.563
abandon your code. and shatter your family.

159
00:15:38.646 --> 00:15:43.117
You see. your team is about to go up
against the only thing they can't handle.

160
00:15:44.152 --> 00:15:45.153
What's that?

161
00:15:47.113 --> 00:15:48.456
You.

162
00:15:49.907 --> 00:15:52.706
Oh. and. Dom. I wouldn't
mention this to anyone.

163
00:15:55.371 --> 00:15:56.714
(ENGINE STARTS)

164
00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:05.344
HOBBS: <i>They are gonna be hitting us
with everything they got.</i>

165
00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:07.638
So we wanna engage with maximum speed.

166
00:16:07.717 --> 00:16:11.096
Neutralize their shooters.
and then move on to our objective.

167
00:16:11.262 --> 00:16:13.310
There's two things
I want you to keep in mind.

168
00:16:13.473 --> 00:16:15.942
Number one. I chose you for this squad

169
00:16:16.017 --> 00:16:19.863
because you are the most fearsome
warriors on the planet.

170
00:16:19.937 --> 00:16:21.985
And number two. you go out there.

171
00:16:22.064 --> 00:16:24.817
you do your job. and you take 'em down.

172
00:16:24.901 --> 00:16:27.120
Everyone.
And I mean everyone.

173
00:16:27.904 --> 00:16:30.748
Mani's and pedi's
at the mall later on today.

174
00:16:31.073 --> 00:16:32.575
(ALL CHEERING)

175
00:16:33.075 --> 00:16:34.076
Huh?

176
00:16:35.411 --> 00:16:36.913
(WHISTLE BLOWING)
GIRLS: Monarchs!

177
00:16:38.789 --> 00:16:40.962
(CHANTING HAKA)

178
00:17:00.102 --> 00:17:02.525
(ALL CHANTING HAKA)

179
00:17:18.246 --> 00:17:19.589
(EXCLAIMS)

180
00:17:22.083 --> 00:17:23.175
(EXHALES SHARPLY)

181
00:17:25.169 --> 00:17:26.170
(WHISPERS) What?

182
00:17:26.295 --> 00:17:27.296
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

183
00:17:30.216 --> 00:17:31.559
I don't wanna play anymore.

184
00:17:33.386 --> 00:17:35.059
All right. let's go. girls.
Let's go. let's go!

185
00:17:35.221 --> 00:17:36.222
Final two minutes.

186
00:17:36.389 --> 00:17:37.390
DS ALLAN: Quite
the cheering section.

187
00:17:40.977 --> 00:17:41.978
HOBBS: Oh. yeah.

188
00:17:42.436 --> 00:17:44.609
Yeah. it's the moms.
They come out to support the kids.

189
00:17:44.772 --> 00:17:47.025
Except there seem to be
more moms than kids.

190
00:17:47.483 --> 00:17:48.609
Way more moms.

191
00:17:50.111 --> 00:17:51.328
(WOMEN GIGGLING)

192
00:17:51.404 --> 00:17:53.702
(CHUCKLES) Yeah.
It's a big soccer town.

193
00:17:54.156 --> 00:17:55.248
Let's go. girls!

194
00:17:55.533 --> 00:17:57.160
So. your intel
was spot-on.

195
00:17:57.368 --> 00:17:59.746
That Damocles 7 EMP weapon
that went missing in the Gulf?

196
00:18:00.037 --> 00:18:02.711
Arms dealers from
the Liberation Front have it in Berlin.

197
00:18:02.832 --> 00:18:03.833
HOBBS: Shit!

198
00:18:03.916 --> 00:18:06.715
This thing can wipe out
an entire electrical grid in a major city.

199
00:18:06.794 --> 00:18:08.216
No lights. no power.

200
00:18:08.379 --> 00:18:09.380
Instant Stone Age.

201
00:18:09.505 --> 00:18:11.758
Chloe. Maya. you can't let her
run by you like that.

202
00:18:11.882 --> 00:18:15.011
- Let's go. let's go! Cross!
- Agent Hobbs. this is a Class Four WMD.

203
00:18:15.094 --> 00:18:16.437
Do you have any idea what's at stake here?

204
00:18:16.512 --> 00:18:19.186
Yes. I know exactly
what is at stake here. okay?

205
00:18:19.307 --> 00:18:21.651
If the Pink Butterflies
beat my Red Dragons.

206
00:18:21.726 --> 00:18:22.898
that means we lose the championship.

207
00:18:24.061 --> 00:18:25.278
Which means I have 20 little girls

208
00:18:25.354 --> 00:18:27.231
who are crying.
and that's not a good thing.

209
00:18:27.315 --> 00:18:30.114
Which then means I have
to spend a lot of time in ice-cream shops

210
00:18:30.192 --> 00:18:31.910
and a lot of time at Tay Tay concerts.

211
00:18:32.486 --> 00:18:33.533
Tay Tay?

212
00:18:34.572 --> 00:18:38.042
Taylor Swift. Gotta be shittin' me.
Get it together. okay?

213
00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.201
Let's go. girls!

214
00:18:39.368 --> 00:18:41.621
We need you to do this.
It's a lot of lives at stake.

215
00:18:41.829 --> 00:18:43.376
All right. but I need to be clear here.

216
00:18:43.706 --> 00:18:46.380
The US government cannot sanction
this operation in any way.

217
00:18:46.626 --> 00:18:47.798
- You're on your own.
- Hey.

218
00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:50.383
If this thing goes sideways.
you don't just get burned.

219
00:18:50.546 --> 00:18:51.763
You go to prison.

220
00:18:52.381 --> 00:18:54.258
And there's nothing
we can do to get you out.

221
00:18:55.509 --> 00:18:56.556
Let me tell you something.

222
00:18:57.053 --> 00:19:02.059
The only thing that I love more
than saving lives is my daughter.

223
00:19:02.224 --> 00:19:05.068
So. if you don't shut up with this
government bullshit right now.

224
00:19:05.227 --> 00:19:07.355
and start showing some team spirit

225
00:19:07.438 --> 00:19:09.907
and respect for the Red Dragons.

226
00:19:10.399 --> 00:19:13.744
I'm gonna have all 20 of them line up
and kick you right in the tay-tay.

227
00:19:16.906 --> 00:19:18.078
Go Dragons!

228
00:19:19.075 --> 00:19:20.201
Say it again.

229
00:19:20.368 --> 00:19:21.585
Go Dragons!

230
00:19:21.744 --> 00:19:23.667
Attaboy. Go Dragons.

231
00:19:24.038 --> 00:19:25.255
Go Dragons.
(CROWD EXCLAIMS)

232
00:19:25.414 --> 00:19:27.667
SAM: I'm open.
She's open! Go. go!

233
00:19:27.958 --> 00:19:30.427
Yes! (LAUGHING)
(WHISTLE BLOWS)

234
00:19:30.586 --> 00:19:32.509
That is my daughter
right there. Yes.

235
00:19:33.422 --> 00:19:34.799
Yes. come here.

236
00:19:34.882 --> 00:19:35.883
How did I do?

237
00:19:36.175 --> 00:19:37.176
Awesome.

238
00:19:37.259 --> 00:19:38.260
Nice job. kid.

239
00:19:41.972 --> 00:19:43.645
(HOBBS SIGHS)
Daddy's gotta go to work?

240
00:19:43.933 --> 00:19:46.277
Uh. yeah.
Daddy's gotta go to work.

241
00:19:46.977 --> 00:19:48.820
Now. you're gonna need
to get a team you can trust.

242
00:19:49.772 --> 00:19:51.069
Oh. I already got one.

243
00:19:57.613 --> 00:19:59.160
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

244
00:20:09.083 --> 00:20:10.300
(SIGHS)

245
00:20:12.294 --> 00:20:13.295
HOBBS: <i>Hey. Dom.</i>

246
00:20:13.629 --> 00:20:14.630
Hey. Hobbs.

247
00:20:14.797 --> 00:20:16.925
<i>I got a job in Berlin and
I need a favor. brother.</i>

248
00:20:19.051 --> 00:20:21.770
No problem. I'll grab the
team and meet you in Berlin.

249
00:20:22.304 --> 00:20:24.306
<i>Thanks. man.
I'll see you soon.</i>

250
00:20:47.955 --> 00:20:48.956
(GRUNTS)

251
00:20:50.833 --> 00:20:53.427
You were only supposed
to create a diversion. Roman.

252
00:20:53.502 --> 00:20:54.594
That was a diversion!

253
00:20:54.670 --> 00:20:56.388
How many of the damn
explosives did you use?

254
00:20:56.839 --> 00:20:58.056
ROMAN: I don't know. Tej.

255
00:20:58.174 --> 00:20:59.676
- All of it?
- Wait. all of it?

256
00:20:59.842 --> 00:21:01.719
Roman. Jesus Christ.

257
00:21:01.844 --> 00:21:03.517
We got more of your fan club ahead.

258
00:21:09.935 --> 00:21:11.027
They're still on us!

259
00:21:11.854 --> 00:21:13.197
These guys are taking this personal.

260
00:21:13.522 --> 00:21:16.617
Roman. we just blew up their
facility and stole their EMP.

261
00:21:16.692 --> 00:21:18.490
Other than your doctor's cold finger.

262
00:21:18.569 --> 00:21:20.446
I'd say it's about as
personal as it can get.

263
00:21:20.863 --> 00:21:21.989
Phase Two!

264
00:21:22.072 --> 00:21:24.700
Phase Two? So you just gonna
keep that to yourself?

265
00:21:24.867 --> 00:21:27.461
What happened to Phase One?
What about that part?

266
00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:29.042
Yeah.
Remember the airplane?

267
00:21:29.205 --> 00:21:30.627
Everyone drove their cars out but you?

268
00:21:31.123 --> 00:21:32.966
I told you. my engine seized up.

269
00:21:33.125 --> 00:21:34.251
It's your balls that seized up.

270
00:21:34.418 --> 00:21:35.590
Just follow my lead. okay?

271
00:21:35.753 --> 00:21:38.176
And. Roman. whatever you do. don't think.

272
00:21:38.589 --> 00:21:39.590
Huh?

273
00:21:39.799 --> 00:21:40.971
Tej. drop it!

274
00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:42.676
Bombs away.

275
00:21:43.344 --> 00:21:44.345
(BEEPS)

276
00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:45.767
Split. now!

277
00:21:50.142 --> 00:21:51.394
ROMAN: Holy...

278
00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:52.732
(CURSES IN GERMAN)

279
00:22:06.742 --> 00:22:08.244
ROMAN: (OVER RADIO)
<i>Great plan. Tej.</i>

280
00:22:08.577 --> 00:22:10.671
But just so you know. you missed some.

281
00:22:10.913 --> 00:22:12.415
Oh. just wait for it.

282
00:22:25.094 --> 00:22:27.096
ROMAN: Oh. shit!

283
00:22:28.848 --> 00:22:30.020
I hate you. Tej!

284
00:22:30.432 --> 00:22:31.729
(LAUGHS)

285
00:22:32.268 --> 00:22:33.360
Got your ass.

286
00:22:39.608 --> 00:22:40.700
You good?

287
00:22:43.112 --> 00:22:44.534
I'll see you when it's done.

288
00:22:48.701 --> 00:22:49.827
All right. great job. team.

289
00:22:49.994 --> 00:22:51.746
Let's break off and meet
me at the safe house.

290
00:22:52.955 --> 00:22:54.298
(ENGINE REVVING)

291
00:23:06.677 --> 00:23:07.678
A hell of a job. brother.

292
00:23:07.928 --> 00:23:09.976
When we get back to the
base. the beer's on me.

293
00:23:25.654 --> 00:23:26.951
(GASPING)

294
00:23:32.036 --> 00:23:33.037
(GRUNTS)

295
00:23:34.163 --> 00:23:35.961
You lost your goddamn mind. Toretto?

296
00:23:39.710 --> 00:23:41.303
Toretto. you put hands on that thing.

297
00:23:41.378 --> 00:23:44.006
you're gonna have the whole world
gunning for you. including me.

298
00:23:46.216 --> 00:23:47.433
(DOM GRUNTS)

299
00:23:49.011 --> 00:23:50.263
I don't know what you're doing.

300
00:23:50.346 --> 00:23:52.098
but you better think about this. Toretto.

301
00:23:53.098 --> 00:23:54.725
It ain't too late to stop this.

302
00:24:07.196 --> 00:24:08.539
It is now.

303
00:24:09.365 --> 00:24:11.163
(TIRES SQUEALING)

304
00:24:11.241 --> 00:24:12.413
(SIRENS BLARING)

305
00:24:13.619 --> 00:24:15.713
That sumbitch just crossed us.

306
00:24:16.038 --> 00:24:18.132
- What?
- Wait a second. what are you talking about?

307
00:24:18.207 --> 00:24:19.208
Dom took the EMP.

308
00:24:19.375 --> 00:24:20.422
Bullshit.

309
00:24:21.460 --> 00:24:22.461
Where are you?

310
00:24:22.711 --> 00:24:23.803
HOBBS: <i>It's too late for me.
Get outta here.</i>

311
00:24:24.046 --> 00:24:25.798
Saw that look in his eye.

312
00:24:25.881 --> 00:24:27.758
and I've seen that look before.

313
00:24:28.592 --> 00:24:30.720
Dominic Toretto just went rogue.

314
00:25:32.823 --> 00:25:34.791
TEJ: All right. I got
his phone records. y'all.

315
00:25:34.950 --> 00:25:37.328
It's a whole bunch of calls
to untraceable numbers.

316
00:25:37.536 --> 00:25:38.537
ROMAN: Burner phones. right?

317
00:25:38.704 --> 00:25:39.956
TEJ: Nah. scrambler.

318
00:25:40.122 --> 00:25:41.374
Same number. but they got some sort of

319
00:25:41.457 --> 00:25:43.175
micro-router
to bury the signal path.

320
00:25:43.333 --> 00:25:47.133
which means Dom is clearly communicating
with somebody that's above our pay grade.

321
00:25:47.379 --> 00:25:49.097
Look. I don't know Dom as well as you.

322
00:25:49.465 --> 00:25:51.308
but if we just look at the facts.

323
00:25:51.967 --> 00:25:54.470
Dom's been having highly
encrypted conversations

324
00:25:54.636 --> 00:25:56.058
with some mysterious person.

325
00:25:57.806 --> 00:25:59.149
He took out Hobbs.

326
00:25:59.725 --> 00:26:01.477
He stole an EMP.
Now he's disappeared.

327
00:26:02.352 --> 00:26:03.524
So. what are you saying?

328
00:26:03.687 --> 00:26:06.611
Maybe we should consider
the fact that Hobbs is right.

329
00:26:07.316 --> 00:26:08.533
Dom did go rogue.

330
00:26:08.609 --> 00:26:09.735
(CAR DOOR SLAMS)

331
00:26:09.985 --> 00:26:10.986
ROMAN: Letty.

332
00:26:11.153 --> 00:26:13.030
LETTY: Before
you judge the man.

333
00:26:13.197 --> 00:26:16.292
remember. you're breathing right
now because he saved your life.

334
00:26:24.625 --> 00:26:26.627
You just gonna let her bump
your shoulder like that?

335
00:26:27.377 --> 00:26:30.597
I'm just saying.
that was a little aggressive.

336
00:26:33.008 --> 00:26:34.134
What you gonna do. email her?

337
00:26:34.551 --> 00:26:35.552
(SIGHS)

338
00:26:37.554 --> 00:26:38.601
(WHISPERS) Check.

339
00:26:39.389 --> 00:26:41.187
(CELL DOOR BUZZING)

340
00:26:49.733 --> 00:26:50.859
Moment. will you. fellas?

341
00:26:52.277 --> 00:26:53.574
Thank you.

342
00:26:53.737 --> 00:26:55.205
Well. this is an exciting new look.

343
00:26:55.697 --> 00:26:57.870
It's a little tight in
the crotch. as always.

344
00:26:57.950 --> 00:26:58.951
(CHUCKLES)

345
00:26:59.243 --> 00:27:01.291
What boy-band bus
did she fall out of?

346
00:27:01.954 --> 00:27:03.297
It's my new junior associate.

347
00:27:03.455 --> 00:27:05.378
He's working with me on this. All yours.

348
00:27:05.457 --> 00:27:07.926
Mr. Nobody and I have been given the
authority to get you out of this.

349
00:27:08.377 --> 00:27:11.256
All you have to do is agree
to the terms and you're free.

350
00:27:12.422 --> 00:27:14.265
What's training wheels
talking about? What terms?

351
00:27:14.883 --> 00:27:16.476
Confess to your crimes in Berlin.

352
00:27:16.927 --> 00:27:18.804
Treason. international espionage.

353
00:27:18.887 --> 00:27:20.810
massive destruction of civic property.

354
00:27:21.056 --> 00:27:22.649
You do that. we close the case.

355
00:27:23.058 --> 00:27:25.231
- And?
- And the DSS blacklists you.

356
00:27:25.394 --> 00:27:26.737
Germany loves that.

357
00:27:26.895 --> 00:27:28.442
LITTLE NOBODY: Officially.
you will be a criminal.

358
00:27:28.522 --> 00:27:29.523
MR. NOBODY: Wait.
Whoa. whoa. whoa.

359
00:27:29.606 --> 00:27:31.324
You need to work on your
delivery. all right?

360
00:27:31.567 --> 00:27:32.910
Unofficially...

361
00:27:34.403 --> 00:27:36.906
You're off the books.
You come work with me.

362
00:27:38.574 --> 00:27:39.541
I'm not a criminal.

363
00:27:39.616 --> 00:27:41.118
MR. NOBODY: Luke.
come on. Labels.

364
00:27:41.910 --> 00:27:43.253
There is no confession.

365
00:27:43.662 --> 00:27:45.255
There are no backroom deals.

366
00:27:45.330 --> 00:27:47.503
I got myself into this. I'm
gonna get myself out of it.

367
00:27:47.749 --> 00:27:50.047
- You know that.
- I do. and that's what I told him. (SIGHS)

368
00:27:50.294 --> 00:27:51.921
Well. there you have it.

369
00:27:53.213 --> 00:27:54.305
Good luck in the courts. man.

370
00:27:56.967 --> 00:27:57.968
What about your daughter?

371
00:28:00.929 --> 00:28:03.182
You know. if you're not gonna
do it for your country.

372
00:28:03.265 --> 00:28:04.266
at least do it for your kid.

373
00:28:04.391 --> 00:28:06.064
(CHUCKLES)
Big mistake. kid.

374
00:28:07.311 --> 00:28:08.483
(EXCLAIMS)

375
00:28:08.562 --> 00:28:10.189
Hold on. Luke. Luke.

376
00:28:10.272 --> 00:28:11.990
He's still working from the manual.

377
00:28:12.149 --> 00:28:14.072
I mean. he doesn't even
really know the rules.

378
00:28:14.943 --> 00:28:16.286
Now. come on. give him a break.

379
00:28:16.737 --> 00:28:18.580
(STRAINED)
Give me a break.

380
00:28:18.822 --> 00:28:19.823
Luke.

381
00:28:20.991 --> 00:28:22.208
(GRUNTING)

382
00:28:22.451 --> 00:28:23.452
Appreciate it.

383
00:28:23.577 --> 00:28:24.794
(COUGHING)

384
00:28:25.078 --> 00:28:26.500
It's good to see you. Nobody.

385
00:28:26.663 --> 00:28:27.789
You. too.

386
00:28:30.584 --> 00:28:31.927
Rule number one...

387
00:28:33.295 --> 00:28:34.467
Know your audience.

388
00:28:34.630 --> 00:28:36.849
I gave you your shot.
You shit the bed.

389
00:28:37.007 --> 00:28:38.975
Now I'm gonna show you
how to get this done.

390
00:28:39.468 --> 00:28:41.641
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

391
00:28:47.768 --> 00:28:49.645
You're dead. cop. Dead!

392
00:28:49.811 --> 00:28:52.189
INMATE: I'm gonna slice
some bacon off your back. pig.

393
00:28:53.649 --> 00:28:55.492
DECKARD:
Well. well. well...

394
00:28:55.651 --> 00:28:59.372
Luke Hobbs behind bars.
Would you look at that.

395
00:29:00.364 --> 00:29:02.162
The bent cop got his day.

396
00:29:03.492 --> 00:29:05.290
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

397
00:29:06.119 --> 00:29:07.166
(CELL DOOR BUZZING)

398
00:29:15.504 --> 00:29:16.847
You know. that color looks good on you.

399
00:29:17.005 --> 00:29:19.224
Yeah. it'll look a whole hell of a
lot better with your blood on it.

400
00:29:19.549 --> 00:29:21.222
Yeah. good luck with that. Hercules.

401
00:29:22.010 --> 00:29:23.512
Lawman gone bad. huh?

402
00:29:24.513 --> 00:29:25.810
Such a cliché.

403
00:29:26.848 --> 00:29:28.475
Oh. well. welcome to the club.

404
00:29:29.184 --> 00:29:30.982
I wouldn't get that twisted. son.

405
00:29:31.144 --> 00:29:33.146
We ain't in no club.
we got nothing in common.

406
00:29:33.230 --> 00:29:34.903
And unlike you. I ain't gonna be here long.

407
00:29:35.148 --> 00:29:36.274
What. you bring a shovel. did you?

408
00:29:36.858 --> 00:29:39.327
Because it's 38 feet of steel and concrete.

409
00:29:39.903 --> 00:29:41.120
Or so I've been told.

410
00:29:41.530 --> 00:29:42.827
(DECKARD CHUCKLES)

411
00:29:43.407 --> 00:29:44.704
Better get to digging.

412
00:29:46.034 --> 00:29:47.035
Wanker.

413
00:29:50.122 --> 00:29:51.214
Yeah.

414
00:30:08.515 --> 00:30:09.732
Move.

415
00:30:10.475 --> 00:30:11.943
Say that again.

416
00:30:12.561 --> 00:30:16.316
If I say it again. it'll be to a corpse.

417
00:30:17.733 --> 00:30:18.950
(CHUCKLES)

418
00:30:19.609 --> 00:30:20.952
I'm gonna enjoy this.

419
00:30:21.445 --> 00:30:22.571
CIPHER: Welcome back. Dom.

420
00:30:22.988 --> 00:30:24.035
Nice job out there.

421
00:30:25.824 --> 00:30:27.246
You excited about tonight?

422
00:30:28.785 --> 00:30:29.786
You're going on this?

423
00:30:35.083 --> 00:30:36.426
You're with me. Dom.

424
00:30:46.345 --> 00:30:47.767
Showing me your shoe collection?

425
00:30:48.096 --> 00:30:49.097
Yep.

426
00:30:52.476 --> 00:30:54.274
A pair for every occasion.

427
00:30:54.436 --> 00:30:57.315
You have enough guns in here
to outfit a small army. huh?

428
00:30:57.481 --> 00:30:59.609
Oh. this is just the tip of the iceberg.

429
00:31:02.861 --> 00:31:05.865
You know what I like about you. Dom?
You're a genuine outlaw.

430
00:31:06.156 --> 00:31:08.625
I mean. you're a man
who lives by his own rules.

431
00:31:08.950 --> 00:31:11.544
Which is surprising. because
when I saw you in Cuba.

432
00:31:11.620 --> 00:31:14.874
I heard about a guy who almost
killed you with a motorcycle.

433
00:31:15.123 --> 00:31:17.626
and you let him keep his car?

434
00:31:18.168 --> 00:31:19.795
Oh. that confused you?

435
00:31:20.128 --> 00:31:21.129
Hmm.

436
00:31:22.964 --> 00:31:24.841
'Course I could've taken his car.

437
00:31:25.509 --> 00:31:27.136
But it's about something bigger.

438
00:31:27.844 --> 00:31:29.266
This way...

439
00:31:31.056 --> 00:31:32.057
I changed him.

440
00:31:32.307 --> 00:31:33.809
That's not your responsibility.

441
00:31:34.017 --> 00:31:35.769
- But it's who I am.
- Is it?

442
00:31:36.353 --> 00:31:38.902
Let me ask you something. Dom.
What's the best thing in your life?

443
00:31:40.565 --> 00:31:42.238
- Family.
- No. it's not.

444
00:31:44.319 --> 00:31:45.821
Not if you're being honest.

445
00:31:46.655 --> 00:31:49.374
It's the 10 seconds
between start and finish.

446
00:31:49.449 --> 00:31:51.292
when you're not thinking about anything.

447
00:31:51.660 --> 00:31:54.334
No family. no obligations.

448
00:31:54.496 --> 00:31:55.713
Just you.

449
00:31:56.790 --> 00:31:57.837
Being free.

450
00:32:03.171 --> 00:32:04.218
I gotta tell you.

451
00:32:04.297 --> 00:32:08.473
this whole saving-the-world. Robin Hood
nonsense you've been doing recently?

452
00:32:08.844 --> 00:32:11.222
It's bullshit.
It's not you.

453
00:32:16.768 --> 00:32:18.395
Be who you are.

454
00:32:19.020 --> 00:32:21.022
Why live only a quarter mile at a time

455
00:32:21.106 --> 00:32:23.734
when you can live your whole life that way?

456
00:32:26.778 --> 00:32:28.075
(PANTING)

457
00:32:35.162 --> 00:32:36.254
Is that it?

458
00:32:36.830 --> 00:32:39.333
Is that all those bloated-out
muscles will give ya?

459
00:32:39.833 --> 00:32:41.380
All show and no go.

460
00:32:41.751 --> 00:32:42.843
(GRUNTS)

461
00:32:46.965 --> 00:32:48.308
(GRUNTING)

462
00:32:55.474 --> 00:32:56.566
Oh. I got plenty of go.

463
00:32:56.933 --> 00:32:58.981
You must've misplaced that

464
00:32:59.060 --> 00:33:01.279
when I kicked your arse up and
down that office of yours.

465
00:33:01.354 --> 00:33:02.401
Yeah.

466
00:33:04.357 --> 00:33:06.485
Just like you Brits.
rewriting history. huh?

467
00:33:06.735 --> 00:33:09.955
All I know is. it wasn't me that was
thrown out of a four-story window.

468
00:33:10.071 --> 00:33:11.072
Jumped.

469
00:33:11.156 --> 00:33:14.035
I jumped out of a four-story
window. saving my partner's life.

470
00:33:14.910 --> 00:33:18.255
'Cause where I'm from. we don't
settle fights by throwing bombs.

471
00:33:18.330 --> 00:33:19.877
Well. that's funny. because where I'm from.

472
00:33:19.956 --> 00:33:22.050
we don't need women to run to our rescue.

473
00:33:22.792 --> 00:33:25.636
I mean. do you really believe
you can stand in front of me

474
00:33:26.880 --> 00:33:29.178
and beat me in a straight-up.
old-fashioned fist fight?

475
00:33:29.341 --> 00:33:30.558
Let me tell you something.

476
00:33:31.092 --> 00:33:34.938
Me and you. one-on-one.
no one else around.

477
00:33:35.555 --> 00:33:39.685
I will beat your ass like a Cherokee drum.

478
00:33:42.646 --> 00:33:44.068
Maybe one day we'll find out.

479
00:33:44.606 --> 00:33:46.449
Oh. you better hope that day never comes.

480
00:33:46.525 --> 00:33:48.198
(DOOR BUZZES)

481
00:33:56.368 --> 00:33:59.622
I said no. Mr. Nobody.
I'm not leaving this cell.

482
00:34:00.163 --> 00:34:01.415
I'll get out my way.

483
00:34:01.581 --> 00:34:02.707
(ALARM BLARING)

484
00:34:02.874 --> 00:34:03.875
The right way!

485
00:34:08.755 --> 00:34:10.098
Hey! Why's the door open?
Get back in your cell!

486
00:34:10.173 --> 00:34:11.800
Relax. It's just
a malfunction.

487
00:34:11.967 --> 00:34:13.719
Get back!
HOBBS: Just a malfunction.

488
00:34:13.802 --> 00:34:15.054
(GRUNTING)

489
00:34:23.144 --> 00:34:24.441
(GRUNTING)

490
00:34:25.981 --> 00:34:27.824
Stop him!
Don't let him get away!

491
00:34:28.650 --> 00:34:29.697
(GRUNTING)

492
00:34:30.819 --> 00:34:31.991
(GROANING)

493
00:34:33.113 --> 00:34:34.535
(GRUNTING)

494
00:34:56.803 --> 00:34:58.020
(YELLING)

495
00:35:01.308 --> 00:35:02.434
MILLER: Hobbs!

496
00:35:03.935 --> 00:35:05.778
I've been waiting a long time for this.

497
00:35:06.938 --> 00:35:08.155
Keep waiting. bitch.

498
00:35:08.231 --> 00:35:09.323
(GRUNTS)

499
00:35:12.360 --> 00:35:13.361
(GROANS)

500
00:35:13.445 --> 00:35:15.664
Rubber bullets. Big mistake.

501
00:35:22.245 --> 00:35:23.417
(GROANING)

502
00:35:31.504 --> 00:35:32.505
(YELLS)

503
00:35:48.355 --> 00:35:49.572
(GRUNTING)

504
00:36:13.672 --> 00:36:15.094
(ALL GRUNTING)

505
00:36:30.438 --> 00:36:31.985
(BOTH PANTING)

506
00:36:37.779 --> 00:36:39.952
Well. that took longer than I expected.

507
00:36:42.117 --> 00:36:43.289
HOBBS: <i>Two questions.</i>
MR. NOBODY: <i>Yeah.</i>

508
00:36:43.493 --> 00:36:45.461
- My daughter?
- With your sister.

509
00:36:46.287 --> 00:36:47.880
Toretto?
(CHUCKLES)

510
00:36:47.956 --> 00:36:49.674
It's interesting you ask.

511
00:36:50.625 --> 00:36:53.174
This is my new base.
Welcome to nowhere.

512
00:36:53.753 --> 00:36:55.050
It's a little sterile for you.

513
00:36:55.130 --> 00:36:56.222
(CHUCKLES)

514
00:36:56.297 --> 00:36:58.174
Listen. there's something I
wanna talk to you about after.

515
00:36:58.258 --> 00:36:59.635
Hey. listen. guys.
Thanks...

516
00:36:59.718 --> 00:37:01.891
Whoa. whoa. whoa. What? Handcuffs?
What is this?

517
00:37:02.137 --> 00:37:03.559
It's called abuse of power.

518
00:37:03.638 --> 00:37:04.890
You told me to round them up.

519
00:37:05.098 --> 00:37:06.145
I didn't tell you to hand...

520
00:37:07.308 --> 00:37:09.527
Cut 'em loose. Oh. man.
This is embarrassing.

521
00:37:09.978 --> 00:37:11.480
I'm sorry. guys. really. I...

522
00:37:12.313 --> 00:37:13.656
So. this is how you treat old friends?

523
00:37:13.982 --> 00:37:17.327
TEJ: Friends? We don't even really
know who the hell this guy is.

524
00:37:17.485 --> 00:37:19.487
Doesn't matter who I am. Tej.
I'm. like. nobody. okay?

525
00:37:19.821 --> 00:37:20.993
Nobody. So. then.
who is he?

526
00:37:21.156 --> 00:37:22.874
Him? He's nothing.
He's. like. less than me.

527
00:37:22.949 --> 00:37:25.953
Clearly. we're getting nowhere with nobody.

528
00:37:26.494 --> 00:37:28.963
I've been in here for four
hours. and my ribs are showing.

529
00:37:29.664 --> 00:37:31.792
I don't know about y'all. but I'm out.

530
00:37:33.293 --> 00:37:34.886
- I wouldn't recommend that.
- What?

531
00:37:34.961 --> 00:37:37.464
Well. thanks to your botched Berlin job.

532
00:37:37.547 --> 00:37:39.800
you all made Interpol's
Top 10 Most Wanted list.

533
00:37:39.966 --> 00:37:41.138
Top 10.
MR. NOBODY: Mmm-hmm.

534
00:37:41.843 --> 00:37:42.844
That's all right.

535
00:37:42.927 --> 00:37:45.601
- Well. not you. Roman.
- What do you mean?

536
00:37:45.680 --> 00:37:48.058
You just missed the cut.
You're number 11. so...

537
00:37:48.141 --> 00:37:50.235
- I'm... I missed?
- Yeah.

538
00:37:50.810 --> 00:37:51.857
ROMAN: That's impossible!

539
00:37:52.562 --> 00:37:53.814
What number did they come in at?

540
00:37:54.981 --> 00:37:58.201
Six. eight. nine. ten.

541
00:37:59.360 --> 00:38:00.452
- She's 10?
- Mmm-hmm.

542
00:38:00.528 --> 00:38:02.622
That's impossible. There's
no way she's a 10.

543
00:38:02.781 --> 00:38:04.533
Oh. she's definitely a 10.
(SCOFFS)

544
00:38:05.450 --> 00:38:09.455
How about we focus on someone who we're
not gonna find on anybody's list.

545
00:38:09.621 --> 00:38:11.419
We're awaiting hard confirmation.

546
00:38:11.498 --> 00:38:15.378
but I believe that's the cyber
terrorist known as Cipher.

547
00:38:16.127 --> 00:38:19.381
Wait. no. Cipher's an organization.
Not a person.

548
00:38:19.631 --> 00:38:20.678
Not according to our sources.

549
00:38:20.882 --> 00:38:21.974
What does she want?

550
00:38:22.091 --> 00:38:23.183
No one knows.

551
00:38:23.510 --> 00:38:25.433
Cipher is like a digital act of God.

552
00:38:25.887 --> 00:38:29.892
They... Well. she can manipulate
world systems from the shadows.

553
00:38:29.974 --> 00:38:31.647
Anything that can be hacked
is hers to play with.

554
00:38:31.726 --> 00:38:35.401
And here's the kicker. You'll never
find her linked to any of it.

555
00:38:35.480 --> 00:38:38.734
Her digital identity is scrubbed
every few seconds. worldwide.

556
00:38:38.817 --> 00:38:40.160
So. basically. she's the bogeyman.

557
00:38:40.318 --> 00:38:43.413
Damn. she's one of the hottest
bogeymans I've ever seen.

558
00:38:43.738 --> 00:38:46.366
I mean. if y'all know her.
tell her to get at your boy.

559
00:38:46.449 --> 00:38:48.122
(ROMAN CHUCKLES)
(CLEARS THROAT)

560
00:38:48.493 --> 00:38:50.416
What are you. 12?
ROMAN: That was my shin. mother...

561
00:38:50.578 --> 00:38:54.208
Let's just say. people are scared
of the hacker group Anonymous.

562
00:38:54.374 --> 00:38:55.842
But even Anonymous won't mess with her.

563
00:38:55.917 --> 00:38:58.295
What the hell does any of
this have to do with us?

564
00:38:58.378 --> 00:38:59.470
Probably nothing. Letty.

565
00:38:59.546 --> 00:39:01.014
but I do find it interesting that.

566
00:39:01.089 --> 00:39:02.807
apparently. for some reason.

567
00:39:02.882 --> 00:39:04.884
she's now working with this guy.

568
00:39:19.274 --> 00:39:20.275
(SIGHS)

569
00:39:20.358 --> 00:39:23.988
He's already delivered a fully
operational EMP into her hands.

570
00:39:24.362 --> 00:39:28.242
Detonate that. they can turn any
city in the world into a war zone.

571
00:39:28.658 --> 00:39:31.127
So. then. what is it
you're suggesting we do?

572
00:39:31.202 --> 00:39:32.374
MR. NOBODY:
Maybe we find Dom. huh?

573
00:39:32.537 --> 00:39:33.663
Well. first. let's catch him.

574
00:39:33.746 --> 00:39:35.623
and then figure out why he's turned.

575
00:39:36.082 --> 00:39:38.801
So. y'all want us to track Dom.

576
00:39:38.960 --> 00:39:41.179
Yeah. I know. Roman.
it's kind of a big job.

577
00:39:41.629 --> 00:39:42.721
It's impossible.

578
00:39:42.881 --> 00:39:47.182
Which is why I'm bringing
in an extra pair of hands.

579
00:39:53.349 --> 00:39:55.818
Ah. my day just got
a whole hell of a lot better.

580
00:39:55.977 --> 00:39:57.229
Mr. Nobody.
you wanna tell me why

581
00:39:57.312 --> 00:40:01.783
you just put me in a room with this
tea-and-crumpets eating. criminal sumbitch?

582
00:40:01.858 --> 00:40:04.111
What a big mouth on a small head.

583
00:40:04.193 --> 00:40:06.241
coming from Prisoner 6753.

584
00:40:06.321 --> 00:40:08.415
Don't think we've forgotten
everything that you've done.

585
00:40:08.489 --> 00:40:10.912
We are not teaming up with this guy.

586
00:40:10.992 --> 00:40:13.586
Let's get one thing clear.
I ain't on your team.

587
00:40:14.037 --> 00:40:17.291
I don't care about you. your
crew. or your little family.

588
00:40:17.665 --> 00:40:18.757
I'm here for Cipher.

589
00:40:18.833 --> 00:40:20.676
What are you gonna do. apply for a job?
Head Asshole?

590
00:40:20.919 --> 00:40:23.889
You know. I think that tight T-shirt's
cutting off the circulation to your brain.

591
00:40:23.963 --> 00:40:25.215
You should get a bigger size.

592
00:40:25.924 --> 00:40:29.428
Cipher came to me first. Wanted
me to steal Nightshade for her.

593
00:40:29.510 --> 00:40:31.012
When I said no. she went after my brother.

594
00:40:31.095 --> 00:40:34.315
Ah. yes. brother Owen.
Who could forget him. huh?

595
00:40:34.974 --> 00:40:37.443
Former hell-raiser
and current guest

596
00:40:37.518 --> 00:40:40.112
at a nasty little black site prison.

597
00:40:40.521 --> 00:40:42.444
Cipher corrupted him and left him for dead.

598
00:40:42.523 --> 00:40:43.775
So. if I get a shot to take her down.

599
00:40:43.858 --> 00:40:45.110
believe me. Flex. I'm taking it.

600
00:40:45.193 --> 00:40:47.116
You're taking my boot right up
your ass. is what you're taking.

601
00:40:47.195 --> 00:40:49.948
Guys. guys. The fastest way to
find Cipher is through Toretto.

602
00:40:50.031 --> 00:40:52.454
Now. aside from myself. there's
only two men in the world

603
00:40:52.533 --> 00:40:54.877
that have ever managed to actually
track him down with any success.

604
00:40:54.994 --> 00:40:57.793
And guess what. They're both
standing in front of me right now.

605
00:40:57.872 --> 00:41:00.876
So. like it or not. you two
are gonna work together.

606
00:41:01.876 --> 00:41:03.048
You got that?

607
00:41:05.964 --> 00:41:07.216
I'm gonna take that as a yes.

608
00:41:08.508 --> 00:41:09.976
Am I the only one seeing this?

609
00:41:10.760 --> 00:41:12.182
Oh. this ought to be good.

610
00:41:12.261 --> 00:41:13.433
(MUMBLES)

611
00:41:15.348 --> 00:41:16.474
Use God's Eye.

612
00:41:17.058 --> 00:41:18.526
We put our lives on the line.

613
00:41:18.601 --> 00:41:21.445
running around the world trying
to figure this thing out.

614
00:41:21.521 --> 00:41:22.898
It can find anybody. right?

615
00:41:23.523 --> 00:41:25.025
Let's use it to find Dom.

616
00:41:25.358 --> 00:41:28.362
Roman. that is a great idea.

617
00:41:29.320 --> 00:41:31.743
Did you hear that?
"Great idea."

618
00:41:32.156 --> 00:41:33.578
No. no. no. don't tune it out. Huh?

619
00:41:33.950 --> 00:41:35.827
Mr. Nobody.
let's fire it up. huh?

620
00:41:47.213 --> 00:41:48.931
TEJ: Got him.
He's in London.

621
00:41:51.134 --> 00:41:52.135
Yeah.

622
00:41:52.218 --> 00:41:53.515
(BEEPING)

623
00:41:54.887 --> 00:41:58.266
RAMSEY: Wait. We've got
a second match in Hong Kong.

624
00:41:58.433 --> 00:42:00.936
ROMAN: Beijing and Seoul.

625
00:42:01.019 --> 00:42:02.521
TEJ: And Tokyo.

626
00:42:04.147 --> 00:42:06.946
RAMSEY: And just about every
other major city on the planet.

627
00:42:07.025 --> 00:42:10.529
MR. NOBODY: And so. God's Eye
was where we started.

628
00:42:10.653 --> 00:42:12.496
But Cipher's already created an evasion

629
00:42:12.572 --> 00:42:16.668
that masks their location by pinging
random spots all over the globe.

630
00:42:16.743 --> 00:42:18.336
but it was a good thought. Roman.

631
00:42:19.704 --> 00:42:21.331
So. she's made my program obsolete.

632
00:42:21.414 --> 00:42:23.792
And that. Ramsey. is why you're here.

633
00:42:24.292 --> 00:42:26.761
See. simple solutions aren't
gonna cut it here. slick.

634
00:42:29.088 --> 00:42:30.556
Why you look at me when you say that?

635
00:42:30.965 --> 00:42:33.684
Wait a second. Wait. wait. Simple
solutions might just cut it.

636
00:42:34.135 --> 00:42:37.389
You see. in order for God's Eye to
give off all these false pings.

637
00:42:37.472 --> 00:42:39.395
means they have to be using a FLEA relay.

638
00:42:39.640 --> 00:42:40.641
Watch these two.

639
00:42:40.725 --> 00:42:42.819
Which means it has a
decaying sync randomizer.

640
00:42:42.894 --> 00:42:44.066
Which we can reverse...

641
00:42:44.145 --> 00:42:48.241
And track it back to the originating
source and find Dom's true location.

642
00:42:49.400 --> 00:42:50.697
I'm telling you. they got skills.

643
00:42:51.152 --> 00:42:52.324
That was my idea.

644
00:42:52.862 --> 00:42:54.535
That's what I was saying.
Remember in there?

645
00:42:54.614 --> 00:42:56.207
All right. let's try this.

646
00:43:06.793 --> 00:43:07.840
It's working.

647
00:43:08.252 --> 00:43:11.472
Time you wanna check your manual and
start organizing a force response.

648
00:43:12.507 --> 00:43:13.804
Let's get a hold of
our international assets...

649
00:43:13.883 --> 00:43:15.305
He's still green.

650
00:43:15.384 --> 00:43:17.227
Yeah. like fresh baby shit.

651
00:43:17.303 --> 00:43:19.897
As soon as we have Toretto's
location. I want to mobilize.

652
00:43:22.475 --> 00:43:25.103
Let's get a hold of a better asshole.

653
00:43:25.228 --> 00:43:27.401
No one respects you...
(IMITATES RADIO STATIC) Cover.

654
00:43:27.563 --> 00:43:28.564
Get away from me.

655
00:43:29.357 --> 00:43:30.529
All right. they're not in China.

656
00:43:32.026 --> 00:43:33.027
Or Russia.

657
00:43:34.445 --> 00:43:35.571
Europe's clear.

658
00:43:37.198 --> 00:43:38.916
But this one's not going away.

659
00:43:39.033 --> 00:43:40.330
(BEEPING)

660
00:43:40.576 --> 00:43:41.623
This is interesting.

661
00:43:42.995 --> 00:43:43.996
Why?

662
00:43:44.205 --> 00:43:45.798
(BEEPING RAPIDLY)

663
00:43:45.998 --> 00:43:47.215
Because that's here.

664
00:43:47.959 --> 00:43:49.302
(GRUNTING)

665
00:44:02.014 --> 00:44:03.516
(GRUNTING)

666
00:44:09.480 --> 00:44:10.527
(EXCLAIMS)

667
00:44:16.779 --> 00:44:18.326
(MAN COUGHING)

668
00:44:27.790 --> 00:44:29.337
CIPHER: (ECHOING)
Did you all enjoy that?

669
00:44:29.417 --> 00:44:31.761
Next-generation
concussion grenade.

670
00:44:32.003 --> 00:44:37.100
It scrambles your senses. Don't
worry. it'll wear off in an hour.

671
00:44:37.175 --> 00:44:38.768
(GROANING)
Probably.

672
00:44:39.427 --> 00:44:41.646
Hello. Deckard.
Nice to see you again.

673
00:44:44.515 --> 00:44:47.359
(LAUGHING) Look at this.
body's not even cold. Dom.

674
00:44:47.643 --> 00:44:49.941
Your family's already replacing you.

675
00:44:51.814 --> 00:44:53.782
You chose the losing team.

676
00:44:54.942 --> 00:44:57.491
I guess your brother is smarter than you.

677
00:45:01.449 --> 00:45:02.541
(DECKARD GRUNTING)

678
00:45:26.766 --> 00:45:28.143
(BEEPING)

679
00:45:31.520 --> 00:45:34.023
Smart move. embedding God's
Eye into the mainframe.

680
00:45:34.482 --> 00:45:37.782
Irritating to make me have to come all
the way down here to get it. but...

681
00:45:41.405 --> 00:45:42.531
Let's go.

682
00:45:42.865 --> 00:45:44.583
(ALL GROANING)

683
00:45:49.330 --> 00:45:50.422
Dom!

684
00:45:59.507 --> 00:46:02.932
You're gonna turn your back on family?
Just like that?

685
00:46:38.421 --> 00:46:39.923
Let's go.

686
00:46:59.358 --> 00:47:01.156
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

687
00:47:13.247 --> 00:47:14.419
HOBBS: You okay?

688
00:47:17.877 --> 00:47:18.924
That wasn't him.

689
00:47:22.757 --> 00:47:24.851
I don't know what she's got on him.

690
00:47:25.968 --> 00:47:27.345
but that wasn't Dom.

691
00:47:29.138 --> 00:47:30.515
Brian would know what to do.

692
00:47:30.598 --> 00:47:31.690
No!

693
00:47:35.603 --> 00:47:38.026
We can't bring Brian and Mia into this.

694
00:47:38.606 --> 00:47:39.983
We agreed on that.

695
00:47:42.443 --> 00:47:43.535
ROMAN: I know.

696
00:47:51.577 --> 00:47:53.454
DOM: <i>Back there.
was that for her.</i>

697
00:47:53.621 --> 00:47:56.295
for me. or you?

698
00:47:57.291 --> 00:47:59.669
And was it even necessary?

699
00:48:00.503 --> 00:48:02.505
Necessary?

700
00:48:02.671 --> 00:48:04.093
Nothing is necessary.

701
00:48:04.256 --> 00:48:06.429
Everything is a choice.

702
00:48:06.592 --> 00:48:08.936
And I simply made one.
But so did you.

703
00:48:09.136 --> 00:48:11.309
You could've stopped me.
but you chose not to.

704
00:48:11.472 --> 00:48:13.645
I wonder what Letty thought about that.

705
00:48:16.185 --> 00:48:18.483
The problem with putting
your foot on a tiger's neck

706
00:48:18.646 --> 00:48:20.148
is you can never let it up.

707
00:48:20.606 --> 00:48:24.907
I think I need to remind you
why you chose to be here.

708
00:48:50.094 --> 00:48:51.095
(GASPS)

709
00:48:51.846 --> 00:48:52.972
Elena.

710
00:49:00.354 --> 00:49:01.446
ELENA: Dom?

711
00:49:08.362 --> 00:49:09.864
I'm sorry.

712
00:49:12.491 --> 00:49:13.617
You shouldn't have come.

713
00:49:14.702 --> 00:49:16.875
Nothing could have kept me away.

714
00:49:17.037 --> 00:49:18.539
Now she has the three of us.

715
00:49:19.748 --> 00:49:20.965
(BABY COOING)

716
00:49:25.212 --> 00:49:26.964
Do you wanna see him?

717
00:49:31.218 --> 00:49:32.470
See Papa?

718
00:49:32.553 --> 00:49:33.896
(BABY GURGLING)

719
00:49:35.055 --> 00:49:36.477
See Papa.

720
00:49:40.394 --> 00:49:41.691
Papa.

721
00:49:45.566 --> 00:49:46.818
(COOING)

722
00:49:51.739 --> 00:49:53.787
When I realized I was pregnant.

723
00:49:53.866 --> 00:49:55.834
you had just found out Letty was alive.

724
00:49:57.745 --> 00:50:00.874
So I decided when Letty and you
got back from your honeymoon.

725
00:50:01.040 --> 00:50:02.917
I was going to tell you.

726
00:50:05.169 --> 00:50:08.298
But then she took us
before I had the chance.

727
00:50:08.380 --> 00:50:09.597
(COOS)

728
00:50:13.427 --> 00:50:14.599
His name?

729
00:50:16.222 --> 00:50:17.269
(CONTINUES COOING)

730
00:50:17.348 --> 00:50:19.146
I call him Marcos.

731
00:50:20.684 --> 00:50:22.686
But that's his middle name.

732
00:50:23.854 --> 00:50:27.404
I thought his father should
give him his first name.

733
00:50:36.367 --> 00:50:38.415
I'm sorry. Dom.

734
00:50:39.537 --> 00:50:41.710
There's nothing to be sorry for.

735
00:50:44.500 --> 00:50:45.752
ELENA: Whatever happens.

736
00:50:47.628 --> 00:50:49.551
just save our son.

737
00:50:53.467 --> 00:50:55.185
Your son.

738
00:51:15.948 --> 00:51:17.700
CIPHER: Good visit?

739
00:51:19.994 --> 00:51:22.622
I know. I know
what you're thinking.

740
00:51:24.290 --> 00:51:25.633
I just let the guards go.

741
00:51:25.791 --> 00:51:28.135
so there's only two opponents in the room.

742
00:51:28.502 --> 00:51:31.472
Rhodes has the gun. so
you'll take him out first.

743
00:51:31.630 --> 00:51:32.756
I know you.

744
00:51:33.090 --> 00:51:36.264
And then you're thinking. Elena's a cop.

745
00:51:36.427 --> 00:51:39.647
Maybe the two of you can
fight your way out of here.

746
00:51:39.805 --> 00:51:42.024
(WHISPERS) So much to think about.

747
00:51:42.224 --> 00:51:44.022
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

748
00:51:47.605 --> 00:51:49.528
Let me make it easier for you.

749
00:51:56.196 --> 00:51:58.073
Do with it as you wish.

750
00:52:06.123 --> 00:52:08.342
Have you heard of Choice Theory. Dom?

751
00:52:08.667 --> 00:52:10.169
There is a bunch of axioms.

752
00:52:10.336 --> 00:52:13.010
but only two you really need
to concern yourself with.

753
00:52:13.172 --> 00:52:17.848
One. the only person's behavior
we can control is our own.

754
00:52:18.010 --> 00:52:22.265
And. two. the only thing we can truly
give another person is information.

755
00:52:22.431 --> 00:52:24.354
So. let me give you some.

756
00:52:25.434 --> 00:52:26.902
You see these cameras in here?

757
00:52:28.520 --> 00:52:31.444
The moment you make a move.
highly-paid men with weapons

758
00:52:31.607 --> 00:52:33.951
will make their way into this room

759
00:52:34.026 --> 00:52:36.575
with one very specific instruction.

760
00:52:37.279 --> 00:52:38.906
It's not to save me.

761
00:52:40.574 --> 00:52:42.417
It's to kill your son.

762
00:52:43.702 --> 00:52:45.750
Now. that's a lot of bullets.

763
00:52:45.913 --> 00:52:48.587
and it only takes one
for you to lose everything.

764
00:52:48.749 --> 00:52:51.377
So. I have to ask you.

765
00:52:51.543 --> 00:52:54.843
because I know family
is so important to you.

766
00:52:57.591 --> 00:53:00.470
Is that really a choice you want to make?

767
00:53:04.014 --> 00:53:06.062
Because I'm ready if you are.

768
00:53:09.770 --> 00:53:12.899
If I pull this trigger.
and God knows I want to.

769
00:53:13.899 --> 00:53:15.572
if I killed everyone on this plane.

770
00:53:16.652 --> 00:53:18.654
I still couldn't get in there.

771
00:53:19.655 --> 00:53:22.499
'Cause of your two-man
fail-safe system.

772
00:53:23.534 --> 00:53:25.207
Since I'm alone.

773
00:53:27.788 --> 00:53:30.041
I got no choice!

774
00:53:38.799 --> 00:53:40.972
I didn't think so.

775
00:54:11.749 --> 00:54:14.093
You want to see the old Dom?

776
00:54:16.420 --> 00:54:17.637
Watch.

777
00:54:24.344 --> 00:54:25.641
(SOBBING)

778
00:54:27.014 --> 00:54:28.186
Bitch.

779
00:54:29.683 --> 00:54:31.685
- Don't. don't.
- Sweet dreams.

780
00:54:31.852 --> 00:54:33.024
Please!

781
00:54:36.732 --> 00:54:37.858
LITTLE NOBODY: Damn it.

782
00:54:38.525 --> 00:54:40.698
She wiped it all.
Took God's Eye.

783
00:54:41.528 --> 00:54:44.202
That was the one thing
we could use to find them.

784
00:54:44.364 --> 00:54:45.707
We lost everything.

785
00:54:48.035 --> 00:54:49.036
What do you got. Princess?

786
00:54:50.245 --> 00:54:51.963
Finding Toretto.

787
00:54:52.414 --> 00:54:54.212
But I got a couple of minutes to spare.

788
00:54:54.374 --> 00:54:57.048
if you want me to send you
to the hospital. Again.

789
00:54:57.377 --> 00:54:59.300
(CHUCKLES) Yo. Rules.

790
00:54:59.463 --> 00:55:01.090
First off. that's not my name.

791
00:55:01.381 --> 00:55:03.258
- Little Nobody.
- Don't call me that.

792
00:55:03.425 --> 00:55:04.426
Oh. that's definitely sticking.

793
00:55:04.510 --> 00:55:05.477
Great. Do me a favor

794
00:55:05.552 --> 00:55:07.646
and tell Your Majesty over there
that we're gonna find Toretto.

795
00:55:07.721 --> 00:55:09.473
We find Toretto together as a team.

796
00:55:09.556 --> 00:55:10.773
And when this is all over with.

797
00:55:10.933 --> 00:55:13.311
I'm happy to slap that whisker
biscuit right off his face.

798
00:55:13.477 --> 00:55:15.730
Wait a minute. guys. I think
Deckard's actually onto something.

799
00:55:15.896 --> 00:55:17.148
How do you think Dom and Cipher

800
00:55:17.231 --> 00:55:19.484
got into the country without us knowing?

801
00:55:20.359 --> 00:55:21.406
Ghost flights.

802
00:55:21.568 --> 00:55:24.412
I thought untraceable aircraft was
all Internet conspiracy stuff.

803
00:55:24.488 --> 00:55:25.535
MR. NOBODY: It's not.

804
00:55:25.656 --> 00:55:29.411
Satellites and radar grids
all across the globe

805
00:55:29.576 --> 00:55:31.624
shift like an ocean.

806
00:55:31.787 --> 00:55:33.915
They've got channels that open and close.

807
00:55:34.081 --> 00:55:35.708
And theoretically.
if you know the right people

808
00:55:35.791 --> 00:55:37.088
who know the right patterns...

809
00:55:37.459 --> 00:55:39.928
You can fly right through the blind
spots completely undetected.

810
00:55:40.712 --> 00:55:42.430
So you know where Dom is headed?

811
00:55:42.506 --> 00:55:43.723
(LAPTOP BEEPS)

812
00:55:43.799 --> 00:55:46.393
Yeah. New York.

813
00:55:46.468 --> 00:55:47.515
(CHUCKLES)

814
00:55:48.720 --> 00:55:49.892
You see there. Luke?

815
00:55:50.055 --> 00:55:52.103
You guys are gonna get along just great.

816
00:55:52.307 --> 00:55:56.062
Which proves rule number two.
you never lose everything.

817
00:55:56.228 --> 00:55:57.445
Fire up the chopper.

818
00:55:57.604 --> 00:56:00.073
Well. guys. have a ball in the Big Apple.

819
00:56:23.130 --> 00:56:25.178
ROMAN: <i>And why are we
traveling like this again?</i>

820
00:56:25.340 --> 00:56:27.092
TEJ: <i>Because Dom
took God's Eye.</i>

821
00:56:27.175 --> 00:56:28.927
<i>so we need to stay off the grid.</i>

822
00:56:29.303 --> 00:56:30.805
ROMAN: But like this?

823
00:56:32.973 --> 00:56:34.646
(ALL GRUNTING)

824
00:56:34.933 --> 00:56:36.059
ROMAN: Look here. man.

825
00:56:36.143 --> 00:56:37.486
Before I throw up in my mouth.

826
00:56:37.644 --> 00:56:39.772
let me ask you. what are we doing here?

827
00:56:39.938 --> 00:56:41.485
That's a good question. Roman.

828
00:56:42.816 --> 00:56:44.033
Let me show you.

829
00:56:48.655 --> 00:56:51.158
Welcome to our new base of operations.

830
00:56:51.325 --> 00:56:54.454
No. seriously.
What is this place?

831
00:56:54.620 --> 00:56:57.043
This is heaven.

832
00:57:03.003 --> 00:57:06.223
It's the agency garage.
They call it the Toy Shop.

833
00:57:10.510 --> 00:57:12.353
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

834
00:57:13.430 --> 00:57:15.273
LITTLE NOBODY: This is where
we house every vehicle

835
00:57:15.349 --> 00:57:17.522
seized from drug dealers on the East Coast.

836
00:57:17.684 --> 00:57:19.357
Now. Mr. Nobody said

837
00:57:19.519 --> 00:57:21.772
that if we're gonna have a
chance at catching Dom.

838
00:57:23.190 --> 00:57:25.363
we're gonna have to be damn fast.

839
00:57:26.526 --> 00:57:28.199
Figured this would help.

840
00:57:31.406 --> 00:57:32.783
We got a tank.

841
00:57:32.950 --> 00:57:35.078
750 horsepower.

842
00:57:35.243 --> 00:57:39.089
6.6 liter.
V8 Duramax engine

843
00:57:39.247 --> 00:57:43.218
with an M153 CROWS remotely
operated weapon station on top.

844
00:57:43.377 --> 00:57:45.721
You didn't get this from drug dealers.

845
00:57:45.879 --> 00:57:49.474
LITTLE NOBODY: No. No. that. uh.
the United States Army lent me.

846
00:57:49.716 --> 00:57:51.093
See. the Army's developing
machines like this

847
00:57:51.259 --> 00:57:53.057
that soldiers can drive from a mile away.

848
00:57:53.220 --> 00:57:55.723
so they can stay safe and alive.

849
00:57:55.889 --> 00:57:58.563
But. luckily. there's
a backup driver's seat

850
00:57:58.725 --> 00:58:02.229
for those of us that like
to get more "hands on."

851
00:58:02.396 --> 00:58:04.148
ROMAN: I'm sitting here
wondering this whole time.

852
00:58:04.314 --> 00:58:07.238
will this thing fit in valet
at Cheesecake Factory?

853
00:58:07.401 --> 00:58:09.779
No one is getting
"hands on."

854
00:58:09.945 --> 00:58:12.243
She doesn't go on city streets.

855
00:58:15.534 --> 00:58:18.663
Wow. I'm in love.

856
00:58:20.831 --> 00:58:22.799
Again. no. no.

857
00:58:22.958 --> 00:58:24.835
That's a million-dollar
show car.

858
00:58:24.918 --> 00:58:26.636
The point is to not draw attention.

859
00:58:26.795 --> 00:58:28.797
It's reverse psychology.

860
00:58:28.880 --> 00:58:30.257
Dom would never see it coming.

861
00:58:30.424 --> 00:58:31.676
It's neon orange.

862
00:58:31.842 --> 00:58:34.937
The International Space
Station would see it coming.

863
00:58:35.095 --> 00:58:37.518
Go choose anything less conspicuous.

864
00:58:37.681 --> 00:58:39.354
ROMAN: No. no. no.
Calipers are my...

865
00:58:39.516 --> 00:58:40.688
- This is ridiculous.
- Not happening.

866
00:58:40.767 --> 00:58:42.235
Hey. my man. you can put
that down right there.

867
00:58:42.436 --> 00:58:46.111
This is a gift. a real gift.
I know what you're doing.

868
00:58:46.189 --> 00:58:48.283
(LAUGHS)
I like your beard.

869
00:58:48.442 --> 00:58:50.194
You're Blanta.
Black Santa?

870
00:58:52.112 --> 00:58:54.615
No. I'm serious.
Put it down right there.

871
00:59:21.808 --> 00:59:22.900
What are you doing?

872
00:59:23.060 --> 00:59:25.404
<i>Engine's misfiring.
I gotta check it out.</i>

873
00:59:25.562 --> 00:59:27.189
No. that's not part of the plan. Dom.

874
00:59:27.355 --> 00:59:28.652
DOM: <i>Clearly.</i>

875
00:59:28.815 --> 00:59:31.364
<i>But unless you want the
engine to seize on the job...</i>

876
00:59:32.486 --> 00:59:33.863
You have five minutes.

877
00:59:41.828 --> 00:59:43.580
(MOUTHING) <i>Five minutes.</i>

878
00:59:46.166 --> 00:59:47.338
I want another visual.

879
00:59:55.675 --> 00:59:56.927
I got an ATM.

880
01:00:08.855 --> 01:00:10.107
I don't like this.

881
01:00:23.912 --> 01:00:25.414
I want to see Toretto.

882
01:00:25.580 --> 01:00:27.378
- There are no more cameras.
- Then find something!

883
01:00:27.541 --> 01:00:28.884
Punch in on something reflective.

884
01:00:29.042 --> 01:00:30.965
A car mirror. anything.

885
01:00:41.054 --> 01:00:42.556
Do you know who I am?

886
01:00:42.722 --> 01:00:44.099
It's why I'm here.

887
01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:46.985
Do you know what I'm capable of?

888
01:00:48.603 --> 01:00:50.446
It's why I'm here.

889
01:00:51.398 --> 01:00:53.821
I'll give you until I finish me cuppa.

890
01:00:53.984 --> 01:00:55.782
And I'm fucking thirsty.

891
01:00:55.944 --> 01:00:57.491
I've got limited time.

892
01:00:57.654 --> 01:00:59.577
so I won't take up too much of yours.

893
01:01:00.323 --> 01:01:01.575
Oh. no.

894
01:01:01.908 --> 01:01:05.162
No. you've already taken everything
I have of value. Mr. Toretto.

895
01:01:05.328 --> 01:01:07.751
What more could you possibly want?

896
01:01:08.582 --> 01:01:10.255
To give you something back.

897
01:01:19.801 --> 01:01:20.927
Talk to me.

898
01:01:24.431 --> 01:01:26.104
Something's not right here.

899
01:01:27.267 --> 01:01:31.773
First time I saw my son was
behind a bulletproof glass.

900
01:01:32.981 --> 01:01:36.531
When he reached for me.
I couldn't hold him.

901
01:01:37.944 --> 01:01:39.867
It's the worst pain I ever felt.

902
01:01:41.323 --> 01:01:44.042
I know you know exactly how that feels.

903
01:01:45.994 --> 01:01:48.122
Maybe we could change that.

904
01:01:49.039 --> 01:01:50.541
Now. why do I think

905
01:01:50.707 --> 01:01:55.304
you're about to suggest something
really dodgy. Mr. Toretto?

906
01:02:00.342 --> 01:02:02.310
It's why I'm here.

907
01:02:03.637 --> 01:02:07.141
Jesus. punch in on something. I'm not
liking this. Something's not right.

908
01:02:08.058 --> 01:02:10.481
Rhodes. you close?
RHODES: <i>Yeah.</i>

909
01:02:10.852 --> 01:02:11.853
CIPHER: Go.

910
01:02:12.020 --> 01:02:13.738
The delivery truck's moving.

911
01:02:23.990 --> 01:02:25.037
(MOUTHING) <i>I know.</i>

912
01:02:35.919 --> 01:02:37.796
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING
OVER RADIO)

913
01:02:46.012 --> 01:02:47.355
HOBBS:
"Captain Deckard Shaw

914
01:02:48.723 --> 01:02:51.067
"distinguished himself by acts of gallantry

915
01:02:51.226 --> 01:02:54.355
"at the risk of his life above
and beyond the call of duty.

916
01:02:54.729 --> 01:02:59.075
"His bold actions saved the lives
of hostages and his teammates.

917
01:02:59.234 --> 01:03:02.329
"Recommendation:
Victoria Cross."

918
01:03:02.696 --> 01:03:05.449
Highest honor the British
government has ever given

919
01:03:06.992 --> 01:03:08.369
to a traitor.

920
01:03:10.328 --> 01:03:12.672
Something about this whole thing
that just doesn't add up to me.

921
01:03:12.831 --> 01:03:14.833
Well. that would be
the same kind of funny math

922
01:03:15.000 --> 01:03:19.301
that says a DSS agent who has a
Silver Star for valor stole an EMP.

923
01:03:19.462 --> 01:03:21.430
Sound familiar. huh?

924
01:03:28.596 --> 01:03:29.597
You want to give me a hand?

925
01:03:32.976 --> 01:03:33.977
- On three?
- Yeah.

926
01:03:34.144 --> 01:03:35.566
One. two. three.

927
01:03:35.645 --> 01:03:36.897
(BOTH GRUNTING)

928
01:03:39.607 --> 01:03:40.608
You know what. Twinkle Toes?

929
01:03:40.775 --> 01:03:43.153
In another life. I bet me and you
could've done some serious damage.

930
01:03:44.446 --> 01:03:45.914
- Yeah. we could've.
- Yeah.

931
01:03:47.449 --> 01:03:49.451
Shame I'm gonna have to bounce
your head off the fender

932
01:03:49.534 --> 01:03:50.786
when this is all over.

933
01:03:51.077 --> 01:03:52.624
(MACHINE WHIRRING)

934
01:03:52.912 --> 01:03:55.131
Ah. well. with all due respect. Captain.

935
01:03:55.290 --> 01:03:57.463
when this whole thing is over.
we're gonna find a location.

936
01:03:57.625 --> 01:03:59.377
and I'm gonna knock your teeth
so far down your throat.

937
01:03:59.544 --> 01:04:02.718
you're gonna stick a toothbrush
right up your ass to brush them.

938
01:04:04.924 --> 01:04:06.722
(BOTH LAUGHING)

939
01:04:09.804 --> 01:04:11.021
Give me God's Eye.

940
01:04:11.848 --> 01:04:12.895
God's Eye. active.

941
01:04:13.099 --> 01:04:14.191
Good.

942
01:04:15.185 --> 01:04:16.778
Let's find us a Russian.

943
01:04:17.437 --> 01:04:19.735
I spy with my little eye.

944
01:04:20.148 --> 01:04:22.367
a Minister of Defense.

945
01:04:33.745 --> 01:04:35.463
(SIRENS WAILING)

946
01:04:39.876 --> 01:04:42.129
(MAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

947
01:04:48.802 --> 01:04:50.554
Upload those coordinates to Dom's nav.

948
01:04:50.637 --> 01:04:51.763
Copy that.

949
01:04:58.812 --> 01:04:59.938
(TIRES SQUEALING)

950
01:05:10.281 --> 01:05:11.533
(LAUGHING)

951
01:05:15.036 --> 01:05:16.504
He's in the third car.

952
01:05:17.580 --> 01:05:19.548
(OVER EARPIECE)
<i>It's a Guard Class limousine.</i>

953
01:05:23.711 --> 01:05:25.133
(INDISTINCT CHATTERING)

954
01:05:34.180 --> 01:05:35.227
Where's my team?

955
01:05:35.390 --> 01:05:37.267
- Where's his team?
- There's no sign of them yet.

956
01:05:37.434 --> 01:05:39.027
They're off the grid.

957
01:05:39.102 --> 01:05:41.025
They're probably just
bunkered down somewhere.

958
01:05:41.104 --> 01:05:42.276
DOM: <i>We're closing in on 'em.</i>

959
01:05:44.149 --> 01:05:45.275
You guys ready?

960
01:05:45.442 --> 01:05:47.035
CIPHER: <i>One thing
I can guarantee. Dom.</i>

961
01:05:47.694 --> 01:05:49.412
no one's ready for this.

962
01:05:49.863 --> 01:05:52.867
I want every chip with a zero-day
exploit in a two-mile radius

963
01:05:53.032 --> 01:05:54.375
around that motorcade now.

964
01:05:54.534 --> 01:05:55.877
There's over a thousand of them.

965
01:05:56.202 --> 01:05:57.203
Hack 'em all.

966
01:06:09.757 --> 01:06:11.384
(ENGINE STARTS)

967
01:06:14.846 --> 01:06:16.098
It's zombie time.

968
01:06:23.897 --> 01:06:25.649
I'd buckle up if I were you.

969
01:06:27.525 --> 01:06:28.526
(TIRES SQUEALING)
Hmm?

970
01:06:29.652 --> 01:06:30.869
WOMAN: (YELLS)
What are you doing?

971
01:06:31.571 --> 01:06:32.697
(GRUNTING)

972
01:06:37.785 --> 01:06:38.786
Ah!

973
01:06:39.871 --> 01:06:41.919
(CAR ENGINE STARTING)
(HORNS BLARING)

974
01:07:02.936 --> 01:07:04.279
GOD'S EYE TECH:
Safety sensors overridden.

975
01:07:04.354 --> 01:07:05.446
Thank you.

976
01:07:07.774 --> 01:07:08.991
(ENGINE STARTS)

977
01:07:10.652 --> 01:07:11.869
MAN: Whoa.

978
01:07:18.117 --> 01:07:19.790
(TIRES SQUEALING)

979
01:07:20.286 --> 01:07:21.458
(WOMAN SHRIEKING)

980
01:07:21.871 --> 01:07:23.123
(EXCLAIMING)

981
01:07:26.960 --> 01:07:28.212
(YELLS AND GROANS)

982
01:07:28.461 --> 01:07:29.462
Hey!

983
01:07:37.720 --> 01:07:38.812
Target the motorcade.

984
01:07:49.148 --> 01:07:51.150
And here they come.

985
01:07:56.114 --> 01:07:57.206
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

986
01:07:58.408 --> 01:07:59.409
(IN ENGLISH) Ouch.

987
01:08:01.703 --> 01:08:03.171
(GRUNTS)
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

988
01:08:09.085 --> 01:08:10.337
GOD'S EYE TECH: (IN ENGLISH)
Police escort down.

989
01:08:10.712 --> 01:08:12.339
Take out the lead and follow cars.

990
01:08:12.839 --> 01:08:13.886
(ENGINES STARTING)

991
01:08:28.646 --> 01:08:29.693
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

992
01:08:31.649 --> 01:08:33.196
(BOTH GRUNTING)

993
01:08:39.616 --> 01:08:40.788
GOD'S EYE TECH:
Two more down.

994
01:08:40.867 --> 01:08:41.993
They're still under warranty.

995
01:08:42.160 --> 01:08:43.412
(RUSSIAN SECRET SERVICE AGENT
IN RUSSIAN)

996
01:08:52.003 --> 01:08:53.050
(ALL SCREAMING)

997
01:08:57.884 --> 01:08:58.885
(MAN SCREAMING)

998
01:09:08.061 --> 01:09:10.234
OFFICER: (OVER RADIO) <i>We got an
army of cars driving themselves!</i>

999
01:09:10.313 --> 01:09:11.610
<i>Send backup. send SWAT!</i>

1000
01:09:11.689 --> 01:09:13.817
<i>I don't care if you send
the goddamn Boy Scouts.</i>

1001
01:09:13.900 --> 01:09:15.152
<i>just send 'em some help!</i>

1002
01:09:15.234 --> 01:09:16.486
Now. that's Dom.

1003
01:09:22.367 --> 01:09:23.459
(SPEAKS RUSSIAN)

1004
01:09:45.348 --> 01:09:46.850
GOD'S EYE TECH: The motorcade
just turned on Seventh.

1005
01:09:46.933 --> 01:09:48.526
CIPHER: Perfect.
Make it rain.

1006
01:09:48.726 --> 01:09:50.069
(ENGINE STARTS)

1007
01:10:24.804 --> 01:10:25.896
Ah!

1008
01:10:26.097 --> 01:10:27.349
(WOMAN SCREAMS)

1009
01:10:34.605 --> 01:10:35.652
(EXCLAIMS)

1010
01:10:37.400 --> 01:10:38.447
(ALL SCREAMING)

1011
01:10:40.111 --> 01:10:41.112
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1012
