This is your doing.

1113
01:22:19.351 --> 01:22:20.352
My doing?

1114
01:22:25.023 --> 01:22:26.525
BABY TORETTO: (BABBLING)
Da-Dada.

1115
01:22:26.692 --> 01:22:27.944
Dada.

1116
01:22:28.360 --> 01:22:29.577
Da-da.

1117
01:22:30.154 --> 01:22:31.906
Please don't hurt him. I'm begging you.

1118
01:22:31.989 --> 01:22:34.367
I don't want you to beg.

1119
01:22:36.869 --> 01:22:38.337
I want you to learn.

1120
01:22:38.704 --> 01:22:40.047
Learn what?

1121
01:22:41.331 --> 01:22:45.006
I understand why you did what you did.
I really do.

1122
01:22:47.671 --> 01:22:48.797
Da-da.

1123
01:22:51.550 --> 01:22:53.518
But it was the wrong choice.

1124
01:22:54.386 --> 01:22:56.889
This is the consequence of that.

1125
01:22:58.640 --> 01:22:59.641
(MUFFLED SCREAMING) No!

1126
01:22:59.808 --> 01:23:01.560
No! No!

1127
01:23:01.727 --> 01:23:02.979
Wait. wait. wait. Wait.

1128
01:23:04.313 --> 01:23:05.940
Save your son!

1129
01:23:06.356 --> 01:23:07.403
No!

1130
01:23:07.691 --> 01:23:08.692
(GUNSHOTS)

1131
01:23:09.026 --> 01:23:10.448
(CRYING)

1132
01:23:17.117 --> 01:23:18.414
(SHUSHING)

1133
01:23:32.758 --> 01:23:33.884
(EXHALES)

1134
01:23:34.593 --> 01:23:37.096
Can you pull up the footage
from the guy in the alley?

1135
01:23:37.804 --> 01:23:38.896
Traffic cams.

1136
01:23:39.056 --> 01:23:40.057
I got you.

1137
01:23:44.603 --> 01:23:45.650
I knew it.

1138
01:23:46.104 --> 01:23:47.401
I recognize that guy.

1139
01:23:48.357 --> 01:23:49.609
That's Connor Rhodes.

1140
01:23:50.025 --> 01:23:52.699
I met him when I was working
with Shaw's brother.

1141
01:23:52.778 --> 01:23:55.076
He wanted us to get
the Nightshade device for him.

1142
01:23:55.489 --> 01:23:56.706
Connor Rhodes.

1143
01:23:57.533 --> 01:23:59.911
He's also linked to somebody
I'd quite like to forget.

1144
01:23:59.993 --> 01:24:01.495
It's Mose Jakande.

1145
01:24:02.204 --> 01:24:04.172
Warlord who tried to get God's Eye.

1146
01:24:04.248 --> 01:24:06.922
Which means that's twice that Dom
has messed up Cipher's business.

1147
01:24:20.722 --> 01:24:22.224
Everything you're feeling right now.

1148
01:24:22.391 --> 01:24:25.235
this rage. a sense of loss. it's not real.

1149
01:24:26.728 --> 01:24:30.574
It's a survival instinct
wired deep into our brains

1150
01:24:30.649 --> 01:24:33.323
to ensure continuation of the species.

1151
01:24:34.528 --> 01:24:37.998
When early man would visit a watering hole.

1152
01:24:38.073 --> 01:24:39.996
if they didn't watch their child.

1153
01:24:40.075 --> 01:24:42.498
and it got snatched by a crocodile.

1154
01:24:43.537 --> 01:24:49.544
our brains would create a painful
but instructional memory.

1155
01:24:51.003 --> 01:24:52.755
so it would never happen again.

1156
01:24:55.007 --> 01:24:58.102
This idea of "family"
that is so core with you.

1157
01:24:58.260 --> 01:25:00.012
that rules your world.

1158
01:25:02.014 --> 01:25:03.607
it's a biological lie.

1159
01:25:05.350 --> 01:25:07.068
You don't have to accept it.

1160
01:25:09.521 --> 01:25:10.568
I don't.

1161
01:25:13.525 --> 01:25:16.529
Did you really think you could
destroy two of my teams

1162
01:25:16.612 --> 01:25:18.364
without any repercussions?

1163
01:25:19.573 --> 01:25:22.372
I wouldn't have even looked your
way if you hadn't done that.

1164
01:25:22.993 --> 01:25:24.995
You didn't even know you had a kid.

1165
01:25:26.413 --> 01:25:29.917
You can thank me for that and start
doing the job I'm asking you to do.

1166
01:25:30.083 --> 01:25:31.505
Help you start a war.

1167
01:25:31.668 --> 01:25:33.511
Is that what you think I want?

1168
01:25:36.214 --> 01:25:37.466
That's so limited.

1169
01:25:39.217 --> 01:25:41.094
I didn't take that football to start a war

1170
01:25:41.178 --> 01:25:43.897
any more than I took your
son to start a family.

1171
01:25:44.848 --> 01:25:46.725
Taking your son got me the codes.

1172
01:25:47.184 --> 01:25:49.357
The codes will get me the nukes

1173
01:25:49.436 --> 01:25:51.814
and the nukes will get me what I want

1174
01:25:51.897 --> 01:25:56.403
today. tomorrow. and every day after that.

1175
01:25:56.610 --> 01:25:58.078
And what's that?

1176
01:26:00.238 --> 01:26:01.490
Accountability.

1177
01:26:03.950 --> 01:26:06.169
The second I fire off one of those nukes.

1178
01:26:06.244 --> 01:26:09.623
I put the superpowers
of this world on notice that.

1179
01:26:09.706 --> 01:26:11.253
when they cross the line.

1180
01:26:13.752 --> 01:26:16.255
I'm gonna be there
to hold them responsible.

1181
01:26:18.090 --> 01:26:20.058
Because the truth is. Dom.

1182
01:26:20.592 --> 01:26:22.139
to the world out there.

1183
01:26:25.097 --> 01:26:27.691
I am the crocodile at the watering hole.

1184
01:26:34.147 --> 01:26:35.990
We've got one last job to do.

1185
01:26:37.859 --> 01:26:39.111
DOM: Cipher.

1186
01:26:48.578 --> 01:26:49.955
If I were you. I'd kiss my son.

1187
01:26:53.875 --> 01:26:57.596
Because whether you value
it or not. all of this.

1188
01:26:58.380 --> 01:27:01.759
your plane. your security. and you.

1189
01:27:02.759 --> 01:27:04.807
are still on this earth because of him.

1190
01:27:10.642 --> 01:27:13.395
RAMSEY: <i>The problem we've had with tracking
Cipher is there's nothing to trace.</i>

1191
01:27:13.478 --> 01:27:14.946
But now. we have Rhodes' information.

1192
01:27:15.021 --> 01:27:16.864
And we're getting snapshots of his data

1193
01:27:16.940 --> 01:27:18.692
before it's scrubbed off the net.

1194
01:27:18.775 --> 01:27:20.072
That looks like somebody's bank account.

1195
01:27:20.152 --> 01:27:21.449
so why don't we just go ahead...

1196
01:27:21.528 --> 01:27:22.700
It's a longitude.

1197
01:27:23.405 --> 01:27:25.658
Given the fact that
Dom hit a Russian motorcade.

1198
01:27:25.741 --> 01:27:27.994
it's safe to say it's Russia.
Go ahead and bring up the map.

1199
01:27:29.286 --> 01:27:31.254
Good. Let's start here
and run the possibilities.

1200
01:27:31.997 --> 01:27:34.671
Yalta. Poltava...

1201
01:27:34.750 --> 01:27:36.172
It's like they just threw letters together.

1202
01:27:36.501 --> 01:27:37.548
Kronyurt.

1203
01:27:37.627 --> 01:27:38.844
MR. NOBODY: It's "Vladovin."

1204
01:27:39.045 --> 01:27:40.592
- What are you doing here?
- What?

1205
01:27:40.756 --> 01:27:42.554
Told you I was gonna check
in on you from time to time

1206
01:27:42.632 --> 01:27:43.633
to see how you were doin'.

1207
01:27:43.717 --> 01:27:45.185
By the way. not so hot.

1208
01:27:45.802 --> 01:27:48.396
But there's nothing
in Vladovin. It's just ice.

1209
01:27:48.472 --> 01:27:49.644
That's funny.

1210
01:27:49.931 --> 01:27:51.854
Could've sworn there was a
secret Russian naval base

1211
01:27:51.933 --> 01:27:53.856
where they retrofitted Cold War submarines.

1212
01:27:53.935 --> 01:27:56.233
Well. technically.
it's not Russian anymore.

1213
01:27:56.855 --> 01:27:57.856
The base was taken over

1214
01:27:57.939 --> 01:28:00.237
by a terror group of military
separatists about a month ago.

1215
01:28:00.317 --> 01:28:01.944
and the Russians haven't taken it back yet.

1216
01:28:02.027 --> 01:28:04.280
so there is a little
window of opportunity here.

1217
01:28:04.529 --> 01:28:06.873
Russian submarines.
Nuclear football.

1218
01:28:07.032 --> 01:28:10.252
It sounds like everything we do.
our legs gonna be blown off.

1219
01:28:10.410 --> 01:28:13.664
It sounds like you still number
11 on the list. (CHUCKLES)

1220
01:28:14.206 --> 01:28:15.753
It sounds like you've changed

1221
01:28:15.832 --> 01:28:18.255
since your little punk-ass
facial hairs done came in.

1222
01:28:18.376 --> 01:28:19.468
Guys. guys.

1223
01:28:19.544 --> 01:28:21.888
Hey. we gotta call this in.
All the way up the chain.

1224
01:28:21.963 --> 01:28:24.762
That's good thinking. champ.
except unfortunately.

1225
01:28:24.841 --> 01:28:26.889
the Russian Minister of Defense

1226
01:28:26.968 --> 01:28:29.721
got himself involved in a little
incident on US territory.

1227
01:28:29.805 --> 01:28:31.933
and the two governments aren't
talking to each other for a while.

1228
01:28:32.015 --> 01:28:33.642
By the time they do. it'll be too late.

1229
01:28:33.725 --> 01:28:35.523
So. any other suggestions?

1230
01:28:36.353 --> 01:28:38.401
HOBBS: Yeah. I got one.

1231
01:28:39.272 --> 01:28:41.115
How about we just stop them ourselves?

1232
01:28:41.191 --> 01:28:43.068
You're talking about
a Russian military base.

1233
01:28:43.151 --> 01:28:44.323
Separatist.

1234
01:28:44.402 --> 01:28:45.494
Whatever.
It's suicide.

1235
01:28:45.570 --> 01:28:47.038
It's stopping World War III.

1236
01:28:49.157 --> 01:28:50.249
What's it gonna be. rook?

1237
01:28:50.742 --> 01:28:52.836
You gonna close your eyes on this one. too?

1238
01:28:52.994 --> 01:28:54.462
Pray that the apocalypse doesn't come

1239
01:28:54.538 --> 01:28:55.960
knocking on your mama's front door?

1240
01:28:56.665 --> 01:28:59.009
Or. are you gonna saddle up. be a man.

1241
01:28:59.084 --> 01:29:01.587
and save the entire goddamn world?

1242
01:29:07.592 --> 01:29:10.061
You know. I think I figured it out.

1243
01:29:10.345 --> 01:29:11.471
What's that?

1244
01:29:11.638 --> 01:29:13.515
Rule number three.
Which is?

1245
01:29:15.016 --> 01:29:16.108
There are no rules.

1246
01:29:17.352 --> 01:29:18.399
(MR. NOBODY LAUGHS)

1247
01:29:18.478 --> 01:29:21.607
What'd I tell you. Luke?
I knew he'd get it in three.

1248
01:29:21.773 --> 01:29:23.320
LITTLE NOBODY: Aerial
transport leaves in an hour.

1249
01:29:23.400 --> 01:29:25.949
Take whatever vehicle you want.
All bets are off.

1250
01:29:26.152 --> 01:29:27.870
- All bets are off?
- Bets are off?

1251
01:29:27.946 --> 01:29:29.289
<i>Do svidanya!</i>

1252
01:29:55.140 --> 01:29:56.813
Letty. I don't like
telling you this one bit.

1253
01:29:57.309 --> 01:29:58.777
But the game's changed.

1254
01:29:59.311 --> 01:30:02.155
Before. we were just trying to catch
Dom. but now. after all this.

1255
01:30:02.397 --> 01:30:04.149
I want you to know. if I have to.

1256
01:30:05.650 --> 01:30:06.776
I'm gonna put him down.

1257
01:30:09.821 --> 01:30:11.414
Then you might have to take us both down.

1258
01:30:13.158 --> 01:30:14.455
ROMAN: I'm freezing. man.

1259
01:30:14.910 --> 01:30:16.207
(BREATHING HEAVILY)
This ain't for me.

1260
01:30:16.661 --> 01:30:19.210
I come from a different
kind of lifestyle. brah.

1261
01:30:21.374 --> 01:30:24.844
Ladies know me. They know
where I'm at with it.

1262
01:30:26.046 --> 01:30:30.017
I tried to take a piss. I
didn't even recognize myself.

1263
01:30:30.425 --> 01:30:32.678
Man. that's entirely too much information.

1264
01:30:32.844 --> 01:30:33.936
I'm just sayin'.

1265
01:30:34.095 --> 01:30:35.768
Well. one thing's for sure.

1266
01:30:36.681 --> 01:30:39.150
Dom's gotta be either working
with them or making a trade.

1267
01:30:39.225 --> 01:30:40.693
because no one would be this insane

1268
01:30:40.769 --> 01:30:42.362
to hit this place without a damn army.

1269
01:30:43.521 --> 01:30:45.694
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

1270
01:30:47.150 --> 01:30:48.367
HOBBS: Speak of the devil.

1271
01:30:56.368 --> 01:30:59.713
All right. Dom. you're one step
closer to that family reunion.

1272
01:30:59.871 --> 01:31:01.043
400 meters to base.

1273
01:31:01.206 --> 01:31:03.550
Prep the EMP. Let's take
these defenses down.

1274
01:31:12.092 --> 01:31:13.389
(ENGINE REVVING)

1275
01:31:15.345 --> 01:31:16.562
(MAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1276
01:31:41.329 --> 01:31:43.673
(CLAPS) (IN ENGLISH) Gates are open.
Let's get this party started.

1277
01:31:49.045 --> 01:31:50.422
(SOLDIERS YELLING IN RUSSIAN)

1278
01:31:59.931 --> 01:32:01.558
- EMP is recharging.
- How long?

1279
01:32:01.891 --> 01:32:03.108
Sixty seconds.

1280
01:32:03.977 --> 01:32:06.526
All right. Dom. you have one
pulse left in that EMP.

1281
01:32:07.022 --> 01:32:08.649
That sub is heavily insulated.

1282
01:32:08.815 --> 01:32:10.988
You're gonna need to be right
underneath it for this thing to work.

1283
01:32:13.153 --> 01:32:14.450
(TIRES SQUEALING)

1284
01:32:31.296 --> 01:32:32.297
(GRUNTING)

1285
01:32:35.633 --> 01:32:36.725
Come on.

1286
01:32:36.926 --> 01:32:38.928
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1287
01:32:44.059 --> 01:32:45.151
(ALARMS BLARING)

1288
01:32:54.319 --> 01:32:55.320
CIPHER: <i>Yes!</i>

1289
01:32:55.487 --> 01:32:56.989
Two birds with one stone.

1290
01:32:57.155 --> 01:32:58.498
SUPER JET TECH:
We've got control of the sub.

1291
01:32:58.573 --> 01:33:01.247
Dom. we are good.
Head over to the rendezvous.

1292
01:33:01.326 --> 01:33:04.421
Okay. Matty. let's take
this baby for a spin.

1293
01:33:10.085 --> 01:33:11.257
TEJ: Damn!

1294
01:33:11.419 --> 01:33:14.013
I think Cipher just rebooted that
sub to slave its command system.

1295
01:33:14.339 --> 01:33:15.716
What the hell is he talking about?

1296
01:33:15.965 --> 01:33:19.515
In layman's terms. she just
carjacked a submarine.

1297
01:33:21.054 --> 01:33:22.647
We can't let it get away.

1298
01:33:23.389 --> 01:33:24.732
There's the control room.

1299
01:33:25.308 --> 01:33:27.231
If you can get me into that wheelhouse.

1300
01:33:27.310 --> 01:33:29.278
I can tap the network
and counter-hack Cipher.

1301
01:33:29.354 --> 01:33:30.981
Keep it from lowering into the water.

1302
01:33:31.064 --> 01:33:32.941
No. what we need to do
is get me on that sub.

1303
01:33:33.191 --> 01:33:35.193
I find the weapons room
and I can pull the launch chip

1304
01:33:35.276 --> 01:33:36.698
before she can fire any of those nukes.

1305
01:33:36.861 --> 01:33:37.953
That is too crazy.

1306
01:33:38.113 --> 01:33:39.410
What you're saying is too dangerous.

1307
01:33:39.489 --> 01:33:40.536
We'll do both.

1308
01:34:04.931 --> 01:34:05.932
Knock. knock.

1309
01:34:08.351 --> 01:34:09.648
(SOLDIERS YELLING IN RUSSIAN)

1310
01:34:11.020 --> 01:34:13.318
(IN ENGLISH) Five vehicles
just breached the base.

1311
01:34:13.481 --> 01:34:15.154
They just don't give up. do they?

1312
01:34:24.200 --> 01:34:26.794
HOBBS: All right. let's haul ass. team.
Double time. double time!

1313
01:34:27.245 --> 01:34:28.747
(SOLDIERS YELLING IN RUSSIAN)

1314
01:34:31.875 --> 01:34:32.876
(YELLING)

1315
01:34:34.460 --> 01:34:35.837
Letty. let's roll!

1316
01:34:37.130 --> 01:34:38.131
(GROANS)

1317
01:34:38.214 --> 01:34:39.636
Go! Go. go. go!

1318
01:35:15.877 --> 01:35:16.924
CIPHER: <i>Change of plans. Dom.</i>

1319
01:35:17.212 --> 01:35:19.306
I'm sending you new coordinates.
Head there immediately.

1320
01:35:19.672 --> 01:35:21.219
<i>I'm done. I want my son.</i>

1321
01:35:21.299 --> 01:35:22.471
I'll tell you when you're done.

1322
01:35:22.842 --> 01:35:24.185
<i>Your team is in play.</i>

1323
01:35:24.260 --> 01:35:26.638
Now. meet Rhodes and follow my instruction.

1324
01:35:30.975 --> 01:35:31.976
(PANTING)

1325
01:35:32.060 --> 01:35:33.687
I've got you covered! Go!

1326
01:35:36.648 --> 01:35:39.151
Move. move!
Get outta here! Go. go. go!

1327
01:35:42.904 --> 01:35:44.656
(PANTING)

1328
01:35:47.075 --> 01:35:49.169
Okay.
How do you like this?

1329
01:35:49.661 --> 01:35:51.504
(ENGINE POWERING DOWN)

1330
01:35:52.455 --> 01:35:53.581
SUPER JET TECH:
Remote link has been severed.

1331
01:35:53.665 --> 01:35:55.042
CIPHER:
I'll take care of this.

1332
01:35:58.962 --> 01:36:00.305
Hi. Ramsey.

1333
01:36:02.257 --> 01:36:03.930
(ENGINE POWERING UP)

1334
01:36:04.175 --> 01:36:05.427
RAMSEY:
She's regained control.

1335
01:36:05.593 --> 01:36:06.845
Damn it. She's good.

1336
01:36:07.470 --> 01:36:08.471
(DOOR UNLOCKING)

1337
01:36:15.144 --> 01:36:16.521
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1338
01:36:25.822 --> 01:36:26.823
(YELLS)

1339
01:36:33.830 --> 01:36:34.831
(ALL GRUNTING)

1340
01:36:44.132 --> 01:36:45.554
(PANTING)

1341
01:36:48.261 --> 01:36:49.478
TECH: They're entering
the weapons room.

1342
01:36:49.554 --> 01:36:50.601
Oh. that's cute.

1343
01:36:57.228 --> 01:36:58.354
LITTLE NOBODY:
(EXCLAIMS) Pull! Pull!

1344
01:36:58.730 --> 01:37:01.074
Roman. Roman!
We gotta find the chip. go!

1345
01:37:04.610 --> 01:37:05.827
Oh. she's slick.

1346
01:37:06.070 --> 01:37:07.572
Gonna have to do better than that. though.

1347
01:37:09.657 --> 01:37:11.580
Okay. now you're starting to piss me off.

1348
01:37:12.327 --> 01:37:13.328
(GRUNTING)

1349
01:37:23.921 --> 01:37:24.922
(MAN YELLING)

1350
01:37:26.799 --> 01:37:28.893
Ramsey. how much time we talkin' here?

1351
01:37:29.344 --> 01:37:32.393
You're smart. but not smart enough.

1352
01:37:33.306 --> 01:37:34.728
(ENGINE POWERING UP)

1353
01:37:35.892 --> 01:37:36.893
She's locked me out.

1354
01:37:39.103 --> 01:37:40.320
(GRUNTING)

1355
01:37:40.938 --> 01:37:43.361
Tej. I can't stop her. You're
gonna have to pull that chip.

1356
01:37:43.441 --> 01:37:45.569
I can't! This thing's
gone into attack mode!

1357
01:37:45.651 --> 01:37:47.779
<i>The door's not gonna open
until you pull the chip!</i>

1358
01:37:48.821 --> 01:37:51.620
Tej. we got no idea what the
hell we're looking for.

1359
01:37:52.992 --> 01:37:53.993
I got it!

1360
01:37:55.286 --> 01:37:56.629
(ALARM BLARING)

1361
01:37:56.954 --> 01:37:59.423
What in the hell are you guys doin'?

1362
01:38:00.416 --> 01:38:02.464
It wasn't me.
It wasn't me. okay?

1363
01:38:02.543 --> 01:38:04.136
It'll be labeled
"Guidance Go."

1364
01:38:04.337 --> 01:38:06.180
- Guidance Go. Guidance Go...
- Okay. I got somethin'.

1365
01:38:06.255 --> 01:38:07.632
- What?
- It says...

1366
01:38:09.300 --> 01:38:11.769
(SPEAKING GIBBERISH)

1367
01:38:13.763 --> 01:38:14.889
Do you understand that?

1368
01:38:20.061 --> 01:38:21.313
(GROANING)

1369
01:38:23.481 --> 01:38:24.983
(MAN LAUGHING)

1370
01:38:29.821 --> 01:38:30.822
(GROANING)

1371
01:38:32.532 --> 01:38:34.409
(YELLING)
(SPLATTERING)

1372
01:38:35.451 --> 01:38:36.998
(PANTING)

1373
01:38:39.914 --> 01:38:41.382
Wow. Nasty.

1374
01:38:52.718 --> 01:38:53.765
Hmm.

1375
01:38:55.012 --> 01:38:56.355
Quite a show.

1376
01:38:59.434 --> 01:39:00.435
We're arming the nuke.

1377
01:39:03.396 --> 01:39:05.069
(POWERING UP)

1378
01:39:05.815 --> 01:39:06.987
TEJ: (OVER RADIO)
<i>Nuke's going hot!</i>

1379
01:39:07.066 --> 01:39:08.283
<i>She's tryin' to fire this thing!</i>

1380
01:39:08.359 --> 01:39:09.406
Roger that.
We're moving out.

1381
01:39:09.485 --> 01:39:10.486
HOBBS: (OVER RADIO)
<i>Disable the nukes!</i>

1382
01:39:10.570 --> 01:39:12.197
Roman. what are you seeing?
Come on. talk to me.

1383
01:39:12.321 --> 01:39:13.948
I don't see shit.
I'm holding on!

1384
01:39:14.240 --> 01:39:15.241
(RUMBLING)

1385
01:39:15.825 --> 01:39:17.077
And we have a countdown.

1386
01:39:19.537 --> 01:39:20.629
(ALARM BLARING)

1387
01:39:20.705 --> 01:39:22.423
What the hell is goin' on. man?

1388
01:39:22.498 --> 01:39:25.547
<i>We're about to launch a nuclear
missile. is what the hell is goin' on!</i>

1389
01:39:25.626 --> 01:39:26.673
<i>Pull the damn chip!</i>

1390
01:39:27.587 --> 01:39:28.804
(PANTING)

1391
01:39:30.089 --> 01:39:32.467
Countdown. countdown!
Look for a countdown!

1392
01:39:32.550 --> 01:39:33.597
What countdown?

1393
01:39:33.676 --> 01:39:35.303
The missiles need to activate to launch.

1394
01:39:35.386 --> 01:39:37.059
The countdown timer won't be in Russian.

1395
01:39:37.346 --> 01:39:38.347
The countdown...

1396
01:39:38.890 --> 01:39:41.063
Let's show the world what we've got.

1397
01:39:42.643 --> 01:39:43.895
ROMAN: No. no. no!
Don't press that!

1398
01:39:46.397 --> 01:39:47.398
I got it.

1399
01:39:49.567 --> 01:39:51.410
Something's wrong.
It won't launch.

1400
01:39:53.112 --> 01:39:55.615
Get that sub outta there.
Now!

1401
01:39:58.201 --> 01:39:59.748
LITTLE NOBODY:
Move your ass. Roman!

1402
01:39:59.827 --> 01:40:01.204
(PANTING)

1403
01:40:07.710 --> 01:40:08.802
You all right?

1404
01:40:08.878 --> 01:40:10.425
There's nothing all right
about any of this!

1405
01:40:10.880 --> 01:40:12.803
- Let's go!
- What about the missiles?

1406
01:40:14.050 --> 01:40:16.052
We got the chip.
No nukes for her.

1407
01:40:16.135 --> 01:40:18.263
Hell. yeah.
Let's roll.

1408
01:40:22.391 --> 01:40:24.940
Guys. we got company.
A lot of company!

1409
01:40:29.857 --> 01:40:31.029
All right. team. here's the plan.

1410
01:40:31.192 --> 01:40:32.944
There's a sea lock
at the opening of the bay.

1411
01:40:33.152 --> 01:40:34.278
<i>We get there first and close it.</i>

1412
01:40:34.362 --> 01:40:37.286
we can stop the submarine
from escaping into open water

1413
01:40:37.406 --> 01:40:38.828
<i>and disappearing forever.</i>

1414
01:40:40.701 --> 01:40:43.454
I've got the location.
It's 10 miles southwest.

1415
01:40:43.704 --> 01:40:46.173
Ten miles? We're not gonna
make it ten seconds!

1416
01:40:48.334 --> 01:40:50.052
(GUNFIRE)

1417
01:40:52.547 --> 01:40:53.548
Ah!

1418
01:40:53.673 --> 01:40:56.142
No. no. no!
This is not good!

1419
01:40:56.968 --> 01:40:59.391
What's the matter. Roman?
Forgot your snow tires?

1420
01:40:59.679 --> 01:41:01.101
ROMAN: Whoa!

1421
01:41:01.305 --> 01:41:02.898
You lovin' that Lambo now?

1422
01:41:03.266 --> 01:41:05.109
ROMAN: Whoa! Ah!

1423
01:41:07.436 --> 01:41:08.483
(ROMAN EXCLAIMS)

1424
01:41:08.980 --> 01:41:09.981
(SCREAMING)

1425
01:41:12.984 --> 01:41:14.327
CIPHER:
All right. everyone.

1426
01:41:14.402 --> 01:41:15.654
We'll deal with that launch chip later.

1427
01:41:15.736 --> 01:41:18.455
Right now. I want that sub in deep
water where no one can find it.

1428
01:41:18.531 --> 01:41:20.158
Find me the fastest route out of that bay.

1429
01:41:20.241 --> 01:41:21.242
Copy that.

1430
01:41:30.918 --> 01:41:32.340
Why are they shootin' at me?

1431
01:41:32.420 --> 01:41:34.639
Maybe 'cause you're in an orange
Lamborghini. I don't know.

1432
01:41:34.714 --> 01:41:36.512
Shut up. Tej!

1433
01:41:41.846 --> 01:41:43.189
Dom...

1434
01:41:43.264 --> 01:41:45.016
(OVER EARPIECE) <i>Do you really
wanna put that car in gear?</i>

1435
01:41:46.601 --> 01:41:47.602
Do it.

1436
01:41:47.977 --> 01:41:48.978
Huh?

1437
01:41:51.689 --> 01:41:53.111
I didn't think so.

1438
01:41:53.190 --> 01:41:54.487
They're heading for the sea lock.

1439
01:41:54.567 --> 01:41:55.819
They're trying to trap the sub in the bay.

1440
01:41:55.901 --> 01:41:58.825
I should have taken care
of this a long time ago.

1441
01:41:58.904 --> 01:42:01.373
<i>Rhodes. take his team out.</i>

1442
01:42:02.199 --> 01:42:03.416
I'm on it.

1443
01:42:09.123 --> 01:42:10.375
Roman. get in front of me!

1444
01:42:17.214 --> 01:42:18.932
Okay. y'all wanna play rough?

1445
01:42:19.800 --> 01:42:20.801
Now it's my turn.

1446
01:42:35.650 --> 01:42:36.993
Yeah. baby! (LAUGHS)

1447
01:42:37.068 --> 01:42:38.490
(LAUGHS)

1448
01:42:46.077 --> 01:42:48.375
Guys. we got snowmobiles on the right.

1449
01:42:50.539 --> 01:42:51.916
They're gonna flank us!

1450
01:42:56.087 --> 01:42:57.088
No. they ain't!

1451
01:43:03.094 --> 01:43:04.311
Oh. shit!

1452
01:43:08.432 --> 01:43:09.479
(BEEPING)

1453
01:43:18.693 --> 01:43:19.694
Tej!

1454
01:43:19.819 --> 01:43:21.571
Roman. hold tight. I'm on the way!

1455
01:43:26.075 --> 01:43:28.169
I don't wanna
go swimmin'! No!

1456
01:43:34.250 --> 01:43:35.467
Really. Tej?

1457
01:43:38.963 --> 01:43:40.340
Oh. no. no. no!

1458
01:43:44.343 --> 01:43:45.435
Oh. shit!

1459
01:43:48.180 --> 01:43:49.397
Roman. grab your door!

1460
01:43:49.473 --> 01:43:50.565
ROMAN: <i>Tej!</i>

1461
01:43:50.808 --> 01:43:52.105
TEJ: <i>Grab the door. Roman!</i>

1462
01:43:52.184 --> 01:43:53.185
ROMAN: <i>It's so cold!</i>
Shit!

1463
01:43:53.811 --> 01:43:54.812
<i>Oh. shit!</i>

1464
01:44:01.610 --> 01:44:02.827
ROMAN: Whoa!

1465
01:44:03.237 --> 01:44:04.454
- Whoo!
- Yeah!

1466
01:44:05.156 --> 01:44:06.783
What is going on?

1467
01:44:06.866 --> 01:44:07.958
Roman. hang on!

1468
01:44:09.493 --> 01:44:10.494
Tej!

1469
01:44:14.206 --> 01:44:15.799
Get me off of this thing!

1470
01:44:16.167 --> 01:44:17.510
Tej!

1471
01:44:21.005 --> 01:44:22.006
Come on!

1472
01:44:31.891 --> 01:44:33.268
Argh!

1473
01:44:37.021 --> 01:44:39.365
All right.
I've had enough of this shit!

1474
01:44:39.899 --> 01:44:41.276
(GRUNTS AND GROANS)

1475
01:44:43.569 --> 01:44:45.867
(ALL GROANING)

1476
01:44:53.579 --> 01:44:55.206
Number 11. my ass!

1477
01:44:57.875 --> 01:45:00.549
Yo. shrinkage! We got a sub to catch.
Get in!

1478
01:45:14.391 --> 01:45:15.392
What?

1479
01:45:15.476 --> 01:45:16.728
Depressurization alert in the cargo hold.

1480
01:45:16.936 --> 01:45:18.563
Drop it to 10.000 feet.

1481
01:45:19.396 --> 01:45:21.774
I know how much these people mean to you.

1482
01:45:21.857 --> 01:45:23.951
So I will let you pick the first target.

1483
01:45:24.026 --> 01:45:25.744
I don't pick a target from a mile away.

1484
01:45:27.571 --> 01:45:30.074
I stand face to face
and look 'em dead in the eye.

1485
01:45:30.783 --> 01:45:31.909
(CHUCKLES)

1486
01:45:32.243 --> 01:45:33.620
Okay.

1487
01:45:33.702 --> 01:45:34.919
The wife it is.

1488
01:45:42.545 --> 01:45:43.762
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1489
01:45:53.055 --> 01:45:56.025
Nice plane.
I'm gonna enjoy having this.

1490
01:45:56.809 --> 01:45:58.152
Hey. don't go gettin' any ideas.

1491
01:45:58.227 --> 01:45:59.820
You and planes don't have a good history.

1492
01:46:02.314 --> 01:46:03.816
No shit.

1493
01:46:03.899 --> 01:46:06.618
Okay. let's go. Scarface.

1494
01:46:07.278 --> 01:46:08.780
These assholes ain't gonna kill themselves.

1495
01:46:12.491 --> 01:46:14.289
Pull up surveillance right now.

1496
01:46:15.870 --> 01:46:17.167
(COMPUTER TRILLS)

1497
01:46:19.415 --> 01:46:20.792
<i>Surprise.</i>

1498
01:46:22.418 --> 01:46:24.420
You're supposed to be dead.

1499
01:46:34.805 --> 01:46:37.308
(MEN SPEAKING SPANISH)

1500
01:46:40.644 --> 01:46:44.148
We have a security breach in the cargo hold.
Take care of it now.

1501
01:46:46.609 --> 01:46:47.610
(GASPS)

1502
01:46:49.653 --> 01:46:52.577
Jesus. Mum. You're supposed
to avoid the nerves.

1503
01:46:52.656 --> 01:46:54.158
Oh. shut up.
Don't be such a baby.

1504
01:47:00.581 --> 01:47:01.582
Get to the pilot.

1505
01:47:01.665 --> 01:47:03.338
He's got the second key.
Wait for my signal.

1506
01:47:04.001 --> 01:47:05.344
Give Cipher my regards.

1507
01:47:06.462 --> 01:47:08.180
Did Toretto hold up his end of the deal?

1508
01:47:19.892 --> 01:47:22.065
MRS. SHAW: <i>He gave us
this little thing here.</i>

1509
01:47:22.353 --> 01:47:24.355
No. no. no. Don't touch.

1510
01:47:24.980 --> 01:47:26.232
You can track Cipher with this.

1511
01:47:26.315 --> 01:47:29.285
but you can't do this on your own.
There's gotta be two of ya.

1512
01:47:29.360 --> 01:47:31.362
Fine. I've got contacts.

1513
01:47:32.488 --> 01:47:33.956
No. you're gonna take your brother.

1514
01:47:34.031 --> 01:47:35.248
- Oh. dear...
- Yes.

1515
01:47:36.116 --> 01:47:38.289
(ALL GRUNTING)

1516
01:47:39.370 --> 01:47:41.418
Toretto knows where he is.

1517
01:47:41.497 --> 01:47:43.090
He's got this thing.
It can see everything.

1518
01:47:43.165 --> 01:47:45.543
It's like... It's called the
Devil's Bum Hole or something.

1519
01:47:45.626 --> 01:47:46.718
It's called the God's Eye.

1520
01:47:46.794 --> 01:47:47.886
Yeah. well. whatever.

1521
01:47:48.712 --> 01:47:50.259
(GRUNTING)

1522
01:47:50.381 --> 01:47:52.975
There's no way I'm using Owen. all right?

1523
01:47:53.050 --> 01:47:54.768
He's a lost cause.

1524
01:47:54.843 --> 01:47:57.892
He's your brother. Decks.
He's my son.

1525
01:47:58.389 --> 01:47:59.857
He's our family.

1526
01:48:00.724 --> 01:48:03.978
And our family don't die
in bloody cages. (CRYING)

1527
01:48:04.353 --> 01:48:07.482
How can you talk like that about Owen?
I can't believe you.

1528
01:48:07.564 --> 01:48:10.659
You've gone and upset me. You've
really upset your mother.

1529
01:48:10.734 --> 01:48:11.986
Call yourself a brother?
You're...

1530
01:48:12.069 --> 01:48:14.367
Look. come here...
Mum. Okay. okay.

1531
01:48:16.490 --> 01:48:18.413
Every time.

1532
01:48:22.287 --> 01:48:23.288
Owen.

1533
01:48:23.664 --> 01:48:24.881
In position.

1534
01:48:26.417 --> 01:48:27.418
Go.

1535
01:48:29.003 --> 01:48:30.175
I'm in.

1536
01:48:30.713 --> 01:48:32.306
(PANTING)

1537
01:48:45.060 --> 01:48:46.437
(CELL PHONE VIBRATING)

1538
01:48:48.731 --> 01:48:49.903
DECKARD:
<i>I've got the package. Toretto.</i>

1539
01:48:50.941 --> 01:48:52.614
All 12 pounds of him.

1540
01:48:52.985 --> 01:48:54.362
Ah.

1541
01:48:54.445 --> 01:48:57.790
Dada. Dada.

1542
01:49:09.460 --> 01:49:10.677
(BULLET RICOCHETS)
(BOTH GASP)

1543
01:49:13.464 --> 01:49:15.387
You made me miss my shot.

1544
01:49:15.466 --> 01:49:17.309
What you think you're doing?

1545
01:49:19.762 --> 01:49:21.139
Looking at you dead in the eye.

1546
01:49:22.347 --> 01:49:23.644
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1547
01:49:32.191 --> 01:49:33.534
(GAGGING)

1548
01:49:34.151 --> 01:49:35.152
(YELLING)

1549
01:49:40.657 --> 01:49:41.658
(YELLING)

1550
01:49:41.867 --> 01:49:42.914
(GRUNTS)
(NECK SNAPS)

1551
01:49:44.411 --> 01:49:46.334
That was for Elena.

1552
01:49:50.000 --> 01:49:51.001
Rhodes.

1553
01:49:51.168 --> 01:49:52.841
DOM: <i>He's no longer with us.</i>

1554
01:49:53.837 --> 01:49:55.430
<i>Rhodes picked the wrong target.</i>

1555
01:49:56.799 --> 01:50:00.599
Congratulations. Dom.
You just killed your son.

1556
01:50:00.677 --> 01:50:03.521
<i>You're wrong.
I just saved him.</i>

1557
01:50:04.306 --> 01:50:06.525
<i>And you just took your foot
off the tiger's neck.</i>

1558
01:50:15.025 --> 01:50:17.869
All right. governor. it's gonna get noisy.

1559
01:50:19.029 --> 01:50:20.656
This is for your ears.

1560
01:50:23.367 --> 01:50:25.540
(BEEPS) (MUSIC PLAYING OVER HEADPHONES)

1561
01:50:25.619 --> 01:50:26.620
Good?

1562
01:50:27.538 --> 01:50:28.539
(COOS)

1563
01:50:29.581 --> 01:50:30.673
Let's go.

1564
01:50:33.043 --> 01:50:36.217
No! Stop him! Do not let
him get off this plane!

1565
01:50:39.049 --> 01:50:40.596
LITTLE NOBODY:
We got another problem.

1566
01:50:40.676 --> 01:50:42.394
That truck's got enough
missiles to take us all out.

1567
01:50:42.636 --> 01:50:43.762
Then don't give 'em a target.

1568
01:50:43.846 --> 01:50:46.144
Everybody. get in front of us.
line up. and we'll take the hit.

1569
01:50:46.223 --> 01:50:49.147
What? I need to
switch cars right now!

1570
01:51:01.363 --> 01:51:02.706
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

1571
01:51:05.450 --> 01:51:07.623
- Roman. here comes the bad part.
- What?

1572
01:51:10.956 --> 01:51:12.048
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1573
01:51:13.208 --> 01:51:14.300
(WHOOPS)

1574
01:51:14.376 --> 01:51:16.629
Hang in there. guys.
We're almost to the lock.

1575
01:51:16.712 --> 01:51:19.591
It's easy for you to say
when your ass ain't on fire.

1576
01:51:25.095 --> 01:51:26.187
All right. little man.

1577
01:51:26.805 --> 01:51:28.773
this might be a little scary.

1578
01:51:29.183 --> 01:51:30.605
but it's gonna be a lot of fun.

1579
01:51:33.103 --> 01:51:34.480
(BOTH GRUNTING)

1580
01:51:42.070 --> 01:51:43.071
How's the music. good?

1581
01:51:43.155 --> 01:51:44.156
Ah.

1582
01:51:47.284 --> 01:51:48.456
(ALL GROANING)

1583
01:51:56.710 --> 01:51:57.962
They're locking on.

1584
01:51:58.045 --> 01:51:59.513
Sorry. guys. I got no tricks left.

1585
01:51:59.588 --> 01:52:00.555
What do we do now?

1586
01:52:00.631 --> 01:52:02.099
TEJ: <i>We start prayin'!</i>

1587
01:52:24.655 --> 01:52:25.656
Hell. yeah!

1588
01:52:38.418 --> 01:52:39.670
There's Dom!

1589
01:52:43.548 --> 01:52:45.050
What. is this guy on our side now?

1590
01:52:45.133 --> 01:52:47.010
Who the hell cares?
He just saved our ass!

1591
01:52:50.681 --> 01:52:52.558
Good to be riding with you again. man.

1592
01:53:00.357 --> 01:53:01.529
(CHUCKLES)

1593
01:53:05.946 --> 01:53:07.448
Toretto just cleared the way for them.

1594
01:53:07.531 --> 01:53:08.999
Someone. give me something!

1595
01:53:09.074 --> 01:53:10.121
Torpedoes are ready.

1596
01:53:10.200 --> 01:53:11.247
Then launch them!

1597
01:53:24.756 --> 01:53:25.757
Shit.

1598
01:53:29.511 --> 01:53:31.309
- Take the wheel!
- I ain't takin' shit!

1599
01:53:31.388 --> 01:53:32.810
Take the wheel!

1600
01:53:33.307 --> 01:53:34.308
Where you goin'?

1601
01:53:34.933 --> 01:53:35.980
(GROANS)

1602
01:53:36.059 --> 01:53:37.311
This is crazy!

1603
01:53:37.394 --> 01:53:38.611
HOBBS: Speed up!

1604
01:53:41.773 --> 01:53:43.320
- Left and back!
- What?

1605
01:53:43.400 --> 01:53:45.653
Turn the goddamn wheel
to the left really quickly!

1606
01:53:52.659 --> 01:53:53.831
Boom. baby!

1607
01:53:58.081 --> 01:54:00.083
(MEN GRUNTING)

1608
01:54:00.667 --> 01:54:01.759
Goin' for a ride.

1609
01:54:07.257 --> 01:54:08.258
Back in a sec.

1610
01:54:10.719 --> 01:54:14.019
(ALL GRUNTING)

1611
01:54:23.565 --> 01:54:24.942
- Where's that smile?
- Ah.

1612
01:54:25.025 --> 01:54:26.197
There it is.

1613
01:54:31.990 --> 01:54:33.162
You were gonna shoot a baby?

1614
01:54:34.451 --> 01:54:36.579
You sick bastard.

1615
01:54:37.537 --> 01:54:38.709
You're not gonna wanna see this.

1616
01:54:43.126 --> 01:54:44.503
(GRUNTING)

1617
01:54:49.633 --> 01:54:51.226
(SNIFFS)

1618
01:54:52.094 --> 01:54:53.141
Is that you or him?

1619
01:54:54.971 --> 01:54:56.018
(SNIFFS)

1620
01:54:56.098 --> 01:54:57.896
Him. Good.

1621
01:54:58.225 --> 01:54:59.522
The torpedoes missed.

1622
01:54:59.601 --> 01:55:01.353
They're gonna reach the lock
before the sub does.

1623
01:55:01.436 --> 01:55:02.653
The hell they are.

1624
01:55:05.399 --> 01:55:06.742
Get ready for this.

1625
01:55:27.003 --> 01:55:28.004
Oh. shit!

1626
01:55:28.088 --> 01:55:29.431
We're gonna need a bigger truck.

1627
01:55:33.135 --> 01:55:34.387
(LAUGHING)

1628
01:55:40.892 --> 01:55:42.565
It's right under us!
Get out the way!

1629
01:55:45.272 --> 01:55:46.615
(GRUNTING)

1630
01:55:50.193 --> 01:55:51.194
(GRUNTING)

1631
01:55:54.823 --> 01:55:55.915
Get us out of here!

1632
01:55:56.074 --> 01:55:57.621
Why are you always yelling?

1633
01:56:01.580 --> 01:56:02.877
This bitch is crazy!

1634
01:56:02.956 --> 01:56:04.333
Look out!
(GASPS)

1635
01:56:05.417 --> 01:56:06.418
(YELLS)

1636
01:56:10.464 --> 01:56:11.556
That's not good.

1637
01:56:13.008 --> 01:56:14.555
That's not good.

1638
01:56:18.305 --> 01:56:20.228
Please tell me there's
nothing to worry about!

1639
01:56:20.307 --> 01:56:21.729
We got this.

1640
01:56:24.769 --> 01:56:25.770
(YELLS)

1641
01:56:28.398 --> 01:56:29.866
(GRUNTS)
(SIGHS)

1642
01:56:30.275 --> 01:56:31.276
(LAUGHS)

1643
01:56:32.944 --> 01:56:33.945
(PANTING)

1644
01:56:34.362 --> 01:56:35.614
That's my girl.

1645
01:56:42.162 --> 01:56:44.836
The sub's too close.
We ain't making it to the gate in time.

1646
01:56:44.915 --> 01:56:46.132
We're just going to let it get away?

1647
01:56:46.458 --> 01:56:47.926
Not if I know Dom.

1648
01:56:53.006 --> 01:56:54.303
You lose. Dom.

1649
01:56:54.382 --> 01:56:56.726
<i>I destroyed two of your teams.</i>

1650
01:56:56.968 --> 01:56:59.266
<i>I killed your
red-headed boyfriend.</i>

1651
01:56:59.346 --> 01:57:02.475
And I put two killers
on your untraceable plane.

1652
01:57:03.642 --> 01:57:06.395
<i>You lost the minute
you interrupted my honeymoon.</i>

1653
01:57:07.270 --> 01:57:09.113
<i>Now guess who I'm coming for.</i>

1654
01:57:09.689 --> 01:57:11.691
Put a heatseeker on him now.

1655
01:57:13.693 --> 01:57:14.819
(SHOUTS) Now!

1656
01:57:20.158 --> 01:57:21.159
Fire!

1657
01:57:25.497 --> 01:57:27.750
That's a goddamn heatseeker coming at us!

1658
01:57:30.502 --> 01:57:32.880
Peel off!
Head to the shore!

1659
01:57:37.008 --> 01:57:38.851
(BEEPING)
(ENGINE REVVING)

1660
01:57:39.052 --> 01:57:41.805
All right.
Come and get it.

1661
01:57:59.739 --> 01:58:00.865
No. no. no.

1662
01:58:02.742 --> 01:58:04.870
Dive! Dive!

1663
01:58:05.495 --> 01:58:06.712
<i>This...</i>

1664
01:58:06.871 --> 01:58:08.544
This is for my son.

1665
01:58:21.803 --> 01:58:23.055
(GASPS)

1666
01:58:27.851 --> 01:58:28.852
Dom!

1667
01:58:39.404 --> 01:58:40.405
(GRUNTS)

1668
01:59:01.801 --> 01:59:02.848
(GRUNTS)

1669
01:59:24.407 --> 01:59:25.408
(DOOR OPENS)

1670
01:59:25.742 --> 01:59:27.119
(GUNSHOTS)
(MAN GROANS)

1671
01:59:31.539 --> 01:59:32.882
You're out of bullets. Deckard.

1672
01:59:32.957 --> 01:59:35.585
Not like I'm gonna need a gun
to take care of you.

1673
01:59:36.961 --> 01:59:38.463
How did you find me?

1674
01:59:40.548 --> 01:59:41.925
DOM: <i>You want to see
the old Dom?</i>

1675
01:59:43.301 --> 01:59:44.518
(BEEPING)
<i>Watch.</i>

1676
01:59:47.597 --> 01:59:49.065
Resourceful.

1677
01:59:49.599 --> 01:59:51.772
You have a lot to answer for. Cipher.

1678
01:59:52.352 --> 01:59:54.195
What you've put my family through.

1679
01:59:54.604 --> 01:59:56.072
My mother.

1680
01:59:57.440 --> 01:59:59.818
I'm gonna make sure
that never happens again.

1681
02:00:00.527 --> 02:00:01.619
To anyone.

1682
02:00:02.362 --> 02:00:04.706
There is only one flaw in your plan.

1683
02:00:04.781 --> 02:00:05.828
What's that?

1684
02:00:05.907 --> 02:00:08.205
Only one of us has a parachute.

1685
02:00:11.037 --> 02:00:12.254
(WIND WHOOSHING)

1686
02:00:17.127 --> 02:00:18.128
(GRUNTING)

1687
02:00:21.923 --> 02:00:22.924
(GRUNTS)

1688
02:00:29.139 --> 02:00:30.356
(COOING)

1689
02:00:30.807 --> 02:00:32.309
Told you this would be fun.

1690
02:00:36.146 --> 02:00:37.489
Time to land. boys.

1691
02:00:48.074 --> 02:00:49.667
You know I never left you. Letty.

1692
02:00:49.743 --> 02:00:50.995
I know.

1693
02:00:51.411 --> 02:00:53.664
And you know I never will.

1694
02:00:55.165 --> 02:00:56.542
I know.

1695
02:00:58.710 --> 02:00:59.927
(LAUGHS)

1696
02:01:00.628 --> 02:01:01.629
(PANTING)

1697
02:01:06.509 --> 02:01:08.386
I have so much to tell you.

1698
02:01:09.053 --> 02:01:13.058
Yeah. you do.
And you can start with that bitch.

1699
02:01:17.395 --> 02:01:20.695
Now. that's Dominic Toretto.

1700
02:01:22.776 --> 02:01:23.777
Hey. Dom!

1701
02:01:23.860 --> 02:01:25.703
I'm just throwin' it out there.

1702
02:01:26.237 --> 02:01:27.955
we need to get up outta here

1703
02:01:28.031 --> 02:01:31.285
'cause there's all kinda nuclearism
happening under this ice.

1704
02:01:31.367 --> 02:01:34.712
Relax. Without the trigger chips.
those nukes are harmless.

1705
02:01:35.079 --> 02:01:36.831
Okay. So we good. then.

1706
02:01:37.123 --> 02:01:40.047
Let me go on and get
my young selfie levels up.

1707
02:01:40.627 --> 02:01:42.550
You realize this is classified. right?

1708
02:01:42.629 --> 02:01:44.006
Not today.

1709
02:01:44.798 --> 02:01:45.890
(CAMERA CLICKS)

1710
02:01:46.132 --> 02:01:47.179
Unbelievable.

1711
02:01:47.258 --> 02:01:49.761
All right. can we get up outta here. now?
I'm freezin'!

1712
02:02:17.622 --> 02:02:18.794
It's okay.

1713
02:02:19.582 --> 02:02:21.710
Don't worry.
He's gonna be here soon.

1714
02:02:22.085 --> 02:02:23.837
ROMAN: I get it.
Y'all got a lot in common.

1715
02:02:23.920 --> 02:02:26.890
Computer hacks. God's Eye.
geeks. nerd... You know.

1716
02:02:26.965 --> 02:02:28.592
But we got a lot in common. too. right?

1717
02:02:28.675 --> 02:02:29.847
Like what?

1718
02:02:29.926 --> 02:02:33.305
We walk in the room
and we're oozin' sex appeal.

1719
02:02:33.388 --> 02:02:35.641
Me and you. hip to hip. is a problem.

1720
02:02:35.723 --> 02:02:38.146
I'm askin' a real question right now.

1721
02:02:38.226 --> 02:02:41.480
Is it gonna be <i>Revenge of the Nerds</i>

1722
02:02:42.272 --> 02:02:45.947
or <i>The Dark Knight?</i> Huh?

1723
02:02:46.276 --> 02:02:48.244
To be honest. I like both of you.

1724
02:02:48.319 --> 02:02:49.912
(ROMAN AND TEJ EXCLAIMING)

1725
02:02:51.406 --> 02:02:54.330
But just before we get into all of that.

1726
02:02:54.409 --> 02:02:56.207
let me ask you one question.

1727
02:02:56.286 --> 02:02:58.163
You can ask me anything.

1728
02:02:58.246 --> 02:02:59.372
Anything.

1729
02:02:59.455 --> 02:03:00.798
What's my last name?

1730
02:03:03.668 --> 02:03:07.093
When you guys figure it out. then.
I guess you can let me know.

1731
02:03:07.171 --> 02:03:09.845
It's gonna be Parker.
That's all that really matters.

1732
02:03:09.924 --> 02:03:11.267
ROMAN: Jones.
TEJ: Mrs. Parker.

1733
02:03:11.676 --> 02:03:13.644
- Right?
- Hey. Mrs. Parker...

1734
02:03:14.178 --> 02:03:15.179
LETTY: Hey.

1735
02:03:15.263 --> 02:03:16.560
Letty.

1736
02:03:16.639 --> 02:03:18.141
I wanted to thank you.

1737
02:03:18.683 --> 02:03:19.684
No need.

1738
02:03:20.935 --> 02:03:21.936
Well...

1739
02:03:22.270 --> 02:03:24.944
Cipher's still on the loose.
There's been some reports she's in Athens.

1740
02:03:25.023 --> 02:03:27.446
but she won't be nuking
any cities anytime soon.

1741
02:03:27.525 --> 02:03:28.742
Thanks to you guys.

1742
02:03:28.818 --> 02:03:30.912
So. I got you a party favor.

1743
02:03:30.987 --> 02:03:32.580
(MR. NOBODY LAUGHS)
HOBBS: This can't be good.

1744
02:03:32.655 --> 02:03:35.158
Your record's been cleared.
Full reinstatement.

1745
02:03:35.241 --> 02:03:36.788
You've got your job back.

1746
02:03:36.868 --> 02:03:38.370
That is. if you want it.

1747
02:03:41.789 --> 02:03:42.915
If I want?

1748
02:03:42.999 --> 02:03:44.000
Mmm-hmm.

1749
02:03:44.083 --> 02:03:45.676
(LAUGHS)

1750
02:03:50.506 --> 02:03:54.682
You know. after 16 years.
I figure it's time for a little break.

1751
02:03:55.303 --> 02:03:56.475
Wow.

1752
02:03:58.056 --> 02:04:00.024
Daddy's stayin' home.

1753
02:04:01.434 --> 02:04:02.686
(LAUGHS)

1754
02:04:06.522 --> 02:04:07.569
Nobody.

1755
02:04:07.649 --> 02:04:08.696
Keep in touch.

1756
02:04:09.150 --> 02:04:10.743
Ah. Hang on a second.

1757
02:04:11.069 --> 02:04:13.242
This could be interesting.

1758
02:04:18.159 --> 02:04:19.331
(SIGHS) What made you think I'd do it?

1759
02:04:20.536 --> 02:04:21.788
Brotherhood.

1760
02:04:21.871 --> 02:04:25.501
I saw that look you gave Cipher.
knew you wanted revenge.

1761
02:04:25.833 --> 02:04:27.335
Glad I did it.

1762
02:04:30.672 --> 02:04:33.175
I can't believe you went to see my mother.

1763
02:04:34.217 --> 02:04:36.436
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

1764
02:04:48.481 --> 02:04:50.483
All this fuss over you.

1765
02:04:51.150 --> 02:04:52.447
(COOING)

1766
02:04:56.489 --> 02:04:57.911
Yes.

1767
02:05:02.996 --> 02:05:06.091
Elena. I promised to keep our son safe.

1768
02:05:08.251 --> 02:05:10.424
And now. he always will be.

1769
02:05:18.553 --> 02:05:22.854
I wanna introduce you to
the most important person in my universe.

1770
02:05:24.517 --> 02:05:26.940
One who never gave up on me.

1771
02:05:32.608 --> 02:05:33.700
He's beautiful.

1772
02:05:35.445 --> 02:05:37.038
DOM: <i>You've heard me say</i>

1773
02:05:37.572 --> 02:05:39.791
that you never turn your back on family.

1774
02:05:41.743 --> 02:05:45.793
and I wanna thank you all
for never turning your back on me.

1775
02:05:50.376 --> 02:05:51.969
You wanna meet them?

1776
02:05:52.628 --> 02:05:54.130
All right.

1777
02:05:54.964 --> 02:05:56.307
Everyone.

1778
02:05:57.633 --> 02:05:59.055
meet Brian.

1779
02:06:00.136 --> 02:06:01.979
(LAUGHTER. APPLAUSE)

1780
02:06:04.932 --> 02:06:05.933
(COOING)

1781
02:06:08.311 --> 02:06:09.563
HOBBS: To Brian!

1782
02:06:09.645 --> 02:06:11.522
ROMAN: Welcome
to the family. Brian.

1783
02:06:11.606 --> 02:06:14.325
Okay. I guess it's my turn to say grace.

1784
02:06:14.776 --> 02:06:17.279
We thank you for giving us family.

1785
02:06:17.361 --> 02:06:21.741
We sit here in praise.
Thank you for giving us the strength...

